Final MM 0.1% f'cast, 0.1% prev; YY 3.4% f'cast, 3.4% prev Looking Ahead - Events, Auctions, Other Releases (GMT) \u8226\'20\'22 N/A ECB Lagarde, Panetta at Eurogroup/EcoFin meetings in Slovenia (till Sat) \u8226\'20\'22 09:30 \uc2 ECB\uc2  Lagarde press conference in Ljubljana, Slovenia \u8226\'20\'22 09:05 ECB Fernandez-Bollo speaks at Bundesbank conference \u8226\'20\'22 10:10 ECB Elderson speaks at BoE/Greening workshop Commentary and Analysis USD/JPY steadies in Asia after fall with US rates yesterday \u8226\'20\'22 USD/JPY steadies in Asia, 109.70-80 EBS, trading quiet pre-weekend \u8226\'20\'22 Support/bids on dips from area of 109.63 low yesterday, trails down \u8226\'20\'22 Action today just below 100-DMA at 109.81, Ichi cloud 109.87-110.19 above \u8226\'20\'22 Market again seen heavy for now above 110.00, Japanese exporters, others \u8226\'20\'22 Nearby option expiries help contain action today, esp with volume low \u8226\'20\'22 109.40-60 total $491 mln, 109.80-95 $515 mln, 110.00-10 $1.2 bln \u8226\'20\'22 Moves in US yields remain focus, Treasury 10s @1.310%, low o/n 1.287% \u8226\'20\'22 Risk mood good despite Wall Street fall, Nikkei +1.1% @30,347, E-Minis +0.2% \u8226\'20\'22 JPY crosses steady after falls overnight with USD/JPY \u8226\'20\'22 EUR/JPY 129.72-90 EBS, capped pre-130 on E535 mln option expiries at strike \u8226\'20\'22 GBP/JPY 151.73-152.06, AUD/JPY 80.71-81.08, NZD/JPY 77.76-78.19 EUR/USD-Recovers from early dip as risk gets boost from Biden/Xi talks \u8226\'20\'22 EUR/USD opened slightly higher at 1.1824 after muted reaction to \uc2 ECB\uc2  \u8226\'20\'22 It dipped to 1.1819 early Asia before getting support from buoyant risk \u8226\'20\'22 AXJ equity index rose over 0.50% on report Biden and Xi spoke by phone \u8226\'20\'22 EUR/USD edged higher and is settling just around 1.1830 \u8226\'20\'22 Resistance is at the 10-day MA at 1.1838 with sellers tipped at 1.1850 \u8226\'20\'22 Bids are eyed ahead of 1.1800 with support at 21-day MA at 1.1788 \u8226\'20\'22 EUR/USD likely to range trade with the \uc2 ECB\uc2  meeting out of the way AUD/USD-Finds support as risk buoyant on Biden/Xi discussion \u8226\'20\'22 AUD/USD opened 0.7368 after having an inside trading day \u8226\'20\'22 It dipped to 0.7360 in early Asia before finding fresh buyers \u8226\'20\'22 Risk assets were buoyant with AXJ equity index up 0.75% and E-minis +0.15% \u8226\'20\'22 Move higher coincided with reports Biden and Xi spoke by phone \u8226\'20\'22 AUD/USD broke above the 10-day MA and is trading just above 0.7380 \u8226\'20\'22 Resistance is at yesterday's 0.7394 high with sellers tipped around 0.7400 \u8226\'20\'22 Support comes in at the 38.2 of the 0.7106/0.7477 move at 0.7335 GBP/USD-Bid with risk appetite, as the USD softens \u8226\'20\'22 +0.1% as USD dipped, risk bounced on Biden and China's Xi talks \u8226\'20\'22 Trades at the top of a 1.3834-1.3850 range - quiet until the headlines \u8226\'20\'22 Poll - BoE to raise rates in late 2022, or possibly sooner \u8226\'20\'22 Charts; neutral signals at familiar levels as choppy consolidation extends \u8226\'20\'22 21 day Bollinger bands expand, momentum studies 5, 10 & 21 DMAs conflict \u8226\'20\'22 1.3825 200 day moving average and 1.3754 Asian low Thursday initial supports \u8226\'20\'22 1.3862 NY high Thursday then 1.3890 September top first initial resistance EUR/USD range should be a friend in the coming weeks The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did an excellent job of communicating its intentions to the market, judging by the muted response to Thursday's meeting, with EUR/USD recording an inside day by trading a tighter range than on Wednesday. The \uc2 ECB\uc2  remains focussed on the economic recovery and COVID-19 vaccine rollout in Europe, combined with the global impact of the coronavirus. The meeting followed U.S. Federal Reserve Chair \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 's cautious Jackson Hole speech on Aug 27, which suggested he is in no rush to change policy settings. Thus unless there is a dramatic event that alters the outlook, the choppy EUR/USD consolidation seen since early July can certainly extend. Counter-trading the range edges or identifying opportunities within the range should be more profitable than looking for trending moves. The range edges are the 1.1664 August low, with the 1.1673 lower 21-day Bollinger band above, and the double daily July-September top at 1.1909, with the upper 21-day Bollinger band below at 1.1904. EUR/USD often swings between the upper and lower Bollinger bands during periods without a strong trend, pivoting around the 21-day moving average. There was a topside swing in July, a downside one in August and another jump in August-September. A sustained break of 1.1786, 50% of the August-September rise, and the 1.1788 21-DMA would target the 1.1673 lower band. China's yuan boxed in as diverse factors dominate China's yuan has been confined to a narrow trading range as fears of an economic slowdown, an ever-expanding regulatory crackdown and official efforts to prevent rapid appreciation are offset by signs the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is in no rush to ease policy and hopes of an easing in U.S.-Sino tensions. PMI surveys suggesting weaker activity in August and five straight months of slower industrial profit growth had fuelled expectations of further policy support from the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2 . Mixed inflation data this week with factory gate inflation at a 13-year high in August while CPI remains benign did not dispel those expectations. The wide gamut of Chinese regulatory measures continues to weigh on the CNH, with the latest crackdown hitting gaming shares worldwide. Simmering concerns that heavily indebted Evergrande Group could spark broader risks to \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's financial system represent another negative factor. Suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Chinese state banks last week when the onshore yuan rallied to 6.4305 may place a floor under USD/CNY. On the other side of the coin, the USD/CNH rally has recently been capped under 6.4700 as comments from the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  cool expectations of broad near-term policy easing. News Friday that Presidents \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2  spoke by phone for the first time since February is also supporting the CNH. USD/CNH is likely to trade in a 6.4200-6.4700 short-term range within a broader 6.4000-6.5000 band. To read our latest \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  news and analysis services, click on\par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-9-13T04:54:09.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020210910eh9a00itt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw109\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1635\pichgoal600
