cently, the PRC government initiated a series of regulatory actions and statements to regulate business \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in China with little advance notice, including cracking down on illegal activities in the securities market, enhancing supervision over China-based companies listed overseas using variable interest entity structure, adopting new measures to extend the scope of cybersecurity reviews, and expanding the efforts in anti-monopoly enforcement. Since these statements and regulatory actions are new, it is highly uncertain how soon legislative or administrative regulation making bodies will respond and what existing or new laws or regulations or detailed implementations and interpretations will be modified or promulgated, if any, and the potential impact such modified or new laws and regulations will have on our daily business \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the ability to accept foreign investments and list on an U.S. or other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 We are an 'emerging growth company' as defined under federal securities laws and, as such, will be subject to reduced public company reporting requirements. See 'Prospectus Summary- Implications of Being an Emerging Growth Company and a Foreign Private Issuer' for additional information.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investing in our securities involves a high degree of risks, including the risk of losing your entire investment. See 'Risk Factors' beginning on page 14 to read about factors you should consider before buying our ordinary shares.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                                Per Ordinary Shareand Warrant         Total   \par Initial public offering price                  US$                                   US$     \par Underwriting discounts and commissions(1)      US$                                   US$     \par Pro