t is evaluated by considering the borrower's financial condition. The Company uses a proprietary model to assign each franchisee a risk rating. This model uses historical franchisee performance data to identify key factors about a franchisee that are considered most significant in predicting a franchisee's ability to meet its financial obligations. The Company also considers numerous other financial and qualitative factors of the franchisee's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , including capitalization and leverage, liquidity and cash flow, profitability, and credit history with the Company and other creditors.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Company also consider recent trends in delinquencies and defaults, recovery rates and the economic environment in assessing the models used in estimating the allowance for loan losses, and may adjust the allowance for loan losses to reflect factors that may not be captured in the models. In addition, the Company periodically consider whether the use of additional metrics would result in improved model performance and revise the models when appropriate. The provision for loan losses is the periodic expense of maintaining an adequate allowance.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An account is considered delinquent when the related franchisee fails to make a substantial portion of a scheduled payment 3 months after the due date. For purposes of determining impairment, loans are evaluated collectively, as they represent a large group of smaller-balance homogeneous loans, and therefore, are not individually evaluated for impairment.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As these loans are non-interest bearing, the Company recorded a discount to the face amount using an imputed interest rate of 11.75% and 8.46% for the years ended October 31, 2020 and 2019, respectively to reflect the fair value of the loan at origination. The imputed interest rate reflects the borrowing rate in the market under similar terms and duration. Direct costs associated with loan originations are not considered material, and thus, are expensed as incurred.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                                                             October 31,2020   October 31,2019 \par Loan to related franchisees, gross                                          9,974,576         4,897,417 \par Discount based on imputed interest rate of 11.75% and 8.46%, respectively   (1,167,634        )   (411,927   ) \par Loan to related franchisees, net of discount                                8,806,942         4,485,490 \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                                              October 31,2020   October 31,2019 \par Loan to related franchisees, net of discount                 8,806,942         4,485,490 \par Provision for credit losses                                  (498,762          )   (193,634   ) \par Loan to related franchisees, net of discount and allowance   8,308,180         4,291,856 \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The following is a summary of the activity in the allowance for credit loss:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                    October 31,2019   October 31,2019 \par Balance at beginning of year       193,634           168,600 \par Provision                          293,362           52,889 \par Charge-offs                        -                 - \par Recoveries                         -                 (23,172   ) \par Effect of translation adjustment   11,766            (4,683    ) \par Balance at end of year             498,762           193,634 \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Credit loss was $305,128 and $61,277 for the years ended October 31, 2020 and 2019, respectively.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The following is a summary of current and non-current loan receivables, net of allowance for credit losses:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                                                            October 31,2020   October 31,2019 \par Loan to related franchisees