tember 16, 2020. \par          \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SIGNATURES\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The registrant hereby certifies that it meets all of the requirements for filing on Form 20-F/A and that it has duly caused and authorized the undersigned to sign this annual report on its behalf.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2   Zhongchao Inc. \par            \par   By:      /s/Weiguang Yang \par   Name:    Weiguang Yang \par   Title:   Chief Executive Officer(Principal Executive Officer) \par            \par   Dated:   August 6, 2021 \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ZHONGCHAO INC.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TABLE OF CONTENTS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Consolidated Financial Statements                                                                    \par Report of Independent Registered Public Accounting Firm                                              F-2 \par Consolidated Balance Sheets as of December 31, 2020 and 2019                                         F-3 \par Consolidated Statements of Income and Comprehensive Income for the Years Ended December 31, 2020, 2019 and 2018  F-4 \par Consolidated Statements of Changes in Equity for the Years Ended December 31, 2020, 2019 and 2018    F-5 \par Consolidated Statements of Cash Flows for the Years Ended December 31, 2020, 2019, 2018              F-6 \par Notes to Consolidated Financial Statements                                                           F-7 \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 F-1\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New York Office\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 7 Penn Plaza, Suite 830\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New York, NY 10001\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 T 212.279.7900\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 REPORT OF INDEPENDENT REGISTERED PUBLIC ACCOUNTING FIRM\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 To the Shareholders and Board of Directors of Zhongchao Inc.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Opinion on the Financial Statements\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 We have audited the accompanying consolidated balance sheets of Zhongchao Inc. (the 'Company') as of December 31, 2020 and 2019, the related consolidated statements of income and comprehensive income, equity and cash flows for each of the three years in the period ended December 31, 2020, and the related notes (collectively referred to as the 'financial statements'). In our opinion, the financial statements present fairly, in all material respects, the financial position of the Company as of December 31, 2020 and 2019, and the results of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and its cash flows for each of the three years in the period ended December 31, 2020, in conformity with accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Basis for Opinion\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 These financial statements are the responsibility of the Company's management. Our responsibility is to express an opinion on the Company's financial statements based on our audits. We are a public accounting firm registered with the Public Company Accounting Oversight Board (United States) ('PCAOB') and are required to be independent with respect to the Company in accordance with the U.S. federal securities laws and the applicable rules and regulations of the Securities and Exchange Commission and the PCAOB.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 We conducted our audits in accordance with the standards of the PCAOB. Those standards require that we plan and perform the audits to obtain reasonable assurance about whether the financial statements are free of material misstatement, whether due to error or fraud. The Company is not required to have, nor were we engaged to perform, an audit of its internal control over financial reporting. As part of our audits we are required to obtain an understanding of internal control over financial reporting but not for the purpose of expressing an opinion on the effectiveness of the Company's internal control over financial reporting. Accordingly, we express no such opinion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Our audits included performing procedures to assess the risks of material misstatement of the financial statements, whether due to error or fraud, and performing procedures that respond to those risks. Such procedures included examining, on a test basis, evidence regarding the amounts and disclosures in the financial statements. Our audits also included evaluating the accounting principles used and significant estimates made by management, as well as evaluating the overall presentation of the financial statements. We believe that our audits provide a reasonable basis for our opinion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Marcum Bernstein & Pinchuk llp\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 We have served as the Company's auditor since 2019\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New York, New York\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 April 30, 2021\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.marcumbp.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.marcumbp.com}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 F-2\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ZHONGCHAO INC.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CONSOLIDATED BALANCE SHEETS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Expressed in U.S. dollar, except for the number of shares)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                                                                                        December 31,2020                  December 31,2019   \par ASSETS                                                                                                                                                      \par Current Assets                                                                                                                                              \par Cash and cash equivalents                                                                              $                  15,072,947                        $   7,832,552    \par Short-term investments                                                                                                    2,032,928                             -            \par Accounts receivable            