ars from the closing date of the offering. The warrants shall not be redeemable.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The registrant hereby amends this registration statement on such date or dates as may be necessary to delay its effective date until the registrant shall file a further amendment which specifically states that this registration statement shall thereafter become effective in accordance with Section 8(a) of the Securities Act of 1933, as amended, or until the registration statement shall become effective on such date as the Securities and Exchange Commission, acting pursuant to such Section 8(a), may determine.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The information in this preliminary prospectus is not complete and may be changed. We may not sell the securities until the registration statement filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission is effective. This preliminary prospectus is not an offer to sell these securities, and we are not soliciting any offer to buy these securities in any jurisdiction where such offer or sale is not permitted. SUBJECT TO COMPLETION\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PRELIMINARY PROSPECTUS DATED July 2, 2021\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ordinary Shares\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Warrants to Purchase Ordinary Shares\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Jiuzi Holdings Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (incorporated in Cayman Islands)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 We are offering ordinary shares, par value $0.001 per share, and warrants to purchase ordinary shares, or Warrants, at an aggregate assumed offering price of US$ per ordinary share and Warrant which is based on the last reported closing trading price of our ordinary shares on Nasdaq on July , 2021. The ordinary shares and Warrants will be separately issued, but the ordinary shares and Warrants will be issued and sold to purchasers in a combination of one ordinary share and one Warrant to purchase one ordinary share for a combined offering price of US$ . Each Warrant will be immediately exercisable for one ordinary share at an exercise price of US$ per share (not less than 100% of the public offering price of per ordinary share and Warrant sold in this offering) and expire years after the issuance date.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Our ordinary shares are listed on the Nasdaq Capital Market, or the Nasdaq, under the symbol 'JZXN'. On July , 2021, the latest reported sale price of our ordinary shares on the Nasdaq Capital Market was US$ per ordinary share. We do not intend to apply to list the Warrants on any security exchange.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shuibo Zhang, our Chairman of the Board of Directors and Chief Executive Officer, is currently the beneficial owner of 58.38% of our outstanding ordinary shares, of which 100% are directly held by Jiuzi One Limited, an entity 100% owned by Mr. Zhang. Our directors and officers collectively own 63.52% of our outstanding ordinary shares and have controlling interest of our Company. Upon the closing of this offering, our directors and officers will continue to own a combined controlling interest in us, and we will meet the definition of a 'controlled company' under the corporate governance standards for NASDAQ listed companies and we will be eligible to utilize certain exemptions from the corporate governance requirements of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 NASDAQ Stock Market\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 We are an 'emerging growth company' as defined under federal securities laws and, as such, will be subject to reduced public company reporting requirements. See 'Prospectus Summary- Implications of Being an Emerging Growth Company and a Foreign Private Issuer' for additional information.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investing in our securities involves a high degree of risks See 'Risk Factors' beginning on page 8.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                                Per Ordinary Shareand Warrant         Total   \par Initial public offering price                  US$                                   US$     \par Underwriting discounts and commissions(1)      US$                                   US$     \par Proceeds to us, before expenses                US$                                   US$     \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (1) We refer you to 'Underwriting' beginning on page 91 for additional information regarding underwriters' compensation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The offering is being underwritten on a firm commitment basis. We have granted the underwriters an over-allotment option exercisable within 45 days from the date of this prospectus to purchase up to an additional ordinary shares from us at a price of US per ordinary share and/or up to an additional Warrants at a price of US$ per Warrant, less, in each case, underwriting discounts and commissions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Neither the Securities and Exchange Commission nor any other regulatory body has approved or disapproved of these securities or passed upon the accuracy or adequacy of this prospectus. Any representation to the contrary is a criminal offense.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Underwriter expects to deliver the ordinary shares and warrants against payment as set forth under 'Underwriting', on or about , 2021.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sole Book Running Manager\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Maxim Group LLC\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Prospectus dated , 2021.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TABLE OF CONTENTS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                                                                         Page \par                                                                                         \par PROSPECTUS SUMMARY                                                                      1 \par                                                                                         \par SELECTED FINANCIAL DATA                                                                 7 \par                                                                                         \par RISK FACTORS                                                             