\par\par \b \uc2 Yuan dips below key threshold on rising corp dollar demand\b0\par\par\uc2 665 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juni 2021\par 07:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SHANGHAI, June 7 (Reuters) - China's yuan dipped against the\par dollar to just below a key threshold on Monday, weighed by\par rising corporate demand for the greenback ahead of several major\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  meetings.\par     The yuan's recent strength has been supported by broad\par dollar weakness, but any change to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's\par accommodative policy stance could spark market volatility,\par traders said. U.S. inflation data this week may open the door\par for the Fed to talk about tapering and lead to a firmer dollar.\par     Prior to market opening, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China (PBOC)\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 set the midpoint rate at 6.3963 per dollar, 109 pips\par or 0.17% firmer than the previous fix of 6.4072. \par     In the spot market, onshore yuan opened at 6.3969\par per dollar and quickly weakened past the key psychologically\par important 6.4 level before changing hands at 6.4008 at midday,\par 58 pips weaker than the previous late session close.\par     Traders and analysts said yuan expectations were divided\par after Chinese policymakers repeatedly warned investors against\par betting on one-sided moves in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  last week\par raised the reserve requirement ratio on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par deposits for the first time in 14 years.\par     "China's first RRR hike for foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  deposits sent a\par signal that there are enough tools in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's toolbox\par to curb the RMB's one-way movement expectation even though the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  has exited from direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tommy Xie\f28 \uc2 \f2 , head\par of Greater \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  research at \f28 \uc2 \f2 OCBC Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Singapore.\par     Traders added that increasing dollar demand from their\par corporate clients on Monday morning had added downward pressure\par on the yuan, despite ample dollar liquidity.\par     Overseas-listed Chinese companies usually have to make their\par interim dividend payments between May and August, and such\par seasonal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  purchases could pile downward pressure on the yuan.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard Chartered\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects total dividend payments to reach $84\par billion this year.\par     The market, meanwhile, shrugged off China's May trade data,\par which showed imports grew at their fastest pace in 10 years,\par fuelled by surging commodity prices, while export growth missed\par expectations, likely on disruptions caused by COVID-19 cases at\par major ports in the country's south.\par     Policy sources told Reuters China was likely to lean on\par incremental steps to slow the yuan's gains to deter speculators\par and help its exporters, shunning drastic measures that could\par undermine its goal to liberalise the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and boost the\par yuan's global clout.\par     Separately, a former senior official at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par regulator advocated the swift introduction of yuan futures\par trading to improve hedging in a market whose recent trend of\par yuan appreciation has been shaped by a "herd effect".\par \par     By midday, the global dollar index rose to 90.153\par from the previous close of 90.142, while the offshore yuan\par  was trading at 6.3975 per dollar. \par \par     The yuan market at 0400 GMT: \par     \par     ONSHORE SPOT:\par  Item               Current  Previous  Change\par  PBOC midpoint      6.3963   6.4072    0.17%\par                                        \par  Spot yuan          6.4008   6.395     -0.09%\par                                        \par  Divergence from    0.07%              \par  midpoint*                             \par  Spot change YTD                       1.99%\par  Spot change since 2005                29.30%\par  revaluation                           \par  \par     Key indexes:\par      \par  Item            Current     Previous  Change\par                                        \par  Thomson         97.72       97.92     -0.2\par  Reuters/HKEX                          \par  CNH index                             \par  Dollar index    90.153      90.142    0.0\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2% from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par   \par  Instrument            Current   Difference\par                                  from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan    6.3975    0.05%\par         *                        \par  Offshore              6.5519    -2.37%\par  non-deliverable                 \par  forwards                        \par                **                \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore\par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par .\par \par  (Reporting by Winni Zhou and Andrew Galbraith; Editing by\par Jacqueline Wong)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-6-7T06:28:46.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020210607eh6700pum\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw109\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1635\pichgoal600
