ding, futures contracts advising and asset management business and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Hong Kong are subject to extensive regulatory oversight by the SFC. The money lending business and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Hong Kong are also subject to regulatory oversight by the Hong Kong Companies Registry and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Police Force\f28 \uc2 \f2 . These factors may increase our cost of doing business and may be a limiting factor in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and development of such businesses. Regulation in relation to our businesses in Hong Kong is also an ever-changing area of law and is subject to modification by the Hong Kong legislature, government, regulatory and judicial action. As our business has expanded into these regulated areas in Hong Kong, we have been required to devote more time to regulatory matters.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On April 12, 2017, Rifa Futures resolved a disciplinary action with the SFC. The disciplinary action was instituted against Rifa Futures by the SFC under section 194 of the Securities and Futures Ordinance with respect to Rifa Futures' internal control deficiencies during the period between January 1, 2014 and July 31, 2014. Although this disciplinary action has been resolved with the SFC, we cannot guarantee that we will not be challenged by the SFC\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Table of Contents\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 or other governmental authorities in Hong Kong in the future. Failure to comply with any of the laws, rules, regulations, codes or guidelines applicable to our businesses in Hong Kong could lead to adverse consequences including, without limitation, investigations, fines, law suits and other penalties from regulatory agencies, which could materially and adversely affect our \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of such businesses.\f28 \par \par \