   $                                  (1,071,648   )          $   (1,562,855   )        $   (8,412,731    ) \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Revenues\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Our total revenues decreased by $276,695 or 84%, from $330,000 in fiscal 2019 to $53,305 in fiscal 2020. All of our total revenues for both fiscal 2020 and fiscal 2019 generated from third parties and no revenues incurred from related party.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Our total revenues decreased by $4,782,520 or 94%, from $5,112,520 in fiscal 2018 to $330,000 in fiscal 2019. Our total revenues - third parties decreased by $3,541,812 or 91%, from $3,871,812 in fiscal 2018 to $330,000 in fiscal 2019, and a decreased in total revenues - related parties of $1,240,708 or 100%, from $1,240,078 in fiscal year 2018 to $0 in fiscal 2019.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The decrease in revenues was primarily due to the continued business as described in detail in the section titled 'Discontinued Business' starting on page 20. During 2020 and 2019, we developed new products and services using technology derived from the discontinued business. These newly developed products and services have not started to contribute to our revenue stream.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cost of Revenues and Gross Margin\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cost of revenues decreased by $4,522 or 11%, from $43,056 in fiscal 2019 to $38,534 for the fiscal 2020. The decrease of cost of revenue was primarily attributable to in line with decrease of revenues. Gross margin for fiscal 2020 was 28%, as compared to 87% for fiscal 2019. The decreased in gross margin of continuing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was primarily due to higher cost in the wage, payroll taxes and higher overhead costs.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cost of revenues decreased by $1,609,972 or 97%, from $1,653,028 in fiscal 2018 to $43,056 for the fiscal 2019. The decrease of cost of revenue was primarily attributable to in line with decrease of revenues. Gross margin for fiscal 2019 was 87%, as compared to 68% for fiscal 2018.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Selling, General and Administrative expenses\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Selling, general and administrative expenses consist primarily of sales and administrative employee-related expenses, professional fees, travel costs, research and development costs, and other corporate expenses. Selling, general and administrative expenses were $1,027,919 for the year of 2020, a decrease of $341,782, or 25% from December 31, 2019 to December 31, 2020. The decrease in selling, general and administrative expenses was primarily due to decrease in payroll expense, depreciation and amortization expenses, and advertising and marketing expenses, reflecting the down sized of our business in fiscal 2020.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Selling, general and administrative expenses consist primarily of sales and administrative employee-related expenses, professional fees, travel costs, research and development costs, and other corporate expenses. Selling, general and administrative expenses were $1,369,701 for the year of 2019, a decrease of $2,507,171, or 65% from December 31, 2018 to December 31, 2019. The decrease in selling, general and administrative expenses was primarily due to decrease in payroll expense, professional service and consulting fees, depreciation and amortization expenses, and advertising and marketing expenses, reflecting the decreased number of employees required to change our business, and offset by increase in regulatory compliance, auditing and filing primarily due to expenses on the acquisitions of new subsidiaries in fiscal 2019.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Research and Development Expenses\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 We incurred $63,450 and $127,117 in research and development in fiscal 2020 and 2019, respectively. Research and development expenses decreased by $63,667, or 50%, for fiscal 2020 compared to fiscal 2019. Research and development expenses decreased by $901,132, or 88%, for fiscal 2019 compared to fiscal 2018, since the Company closed research and development projects and dismissed most of employees of research in the middle of fiscal 2019.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bad debt expense\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 We did not have expenses in bad debt expense in fiscal 2020 and 2019. We collected all the accounts receivables as of December 31, 2020 and 2019, due to the Company's sales arrangement usually requires advanced payment since fiscal 2018. We incurred $923,217 in bad debt expense in fiscal 2018.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Loss from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 As a result of the factors described above, operating loss was $1,013,149 for fiscal 2020, compared to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  loss was $1,209,874 for fiscal 2019, a decrease in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  loss of $196,725, or 16%. Our \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  loss in fiscal 2019 was $1,209,874, compared to operating income was $2,368,846 for fiscal 2018, a decrease in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  loss of $1,158,971, or 49%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Other expenses\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For fiscal 2020, other expense, net of other income, were $7,656, compared to other expenses, net of other income, were 211,422 for fiscal 2019, a change of $203,766. The decrease of other expense was primarily attributable to a decrease of gain on foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  transactions and other non-operating income. The Company also incurred a non-operating expense on impairment of disposal of $1,517.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For fiscal 2019, other expense, net of other income, were $211,422, compared to other expenses, net of other income, were $12,836 for fiscal 2018, a change of $198,585. The increase of other expense was primarily attributable to a decrease of gain on foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  transactions and offset by a decrease expense of $68,858 incurred in the 2018 periods related to our equity method investment.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Loss from continuing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 As a result of the foregoing, our loss from continuing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was $1,097,148, or $(0.05) per share (basic and diluted), for the year ended December 31, 2020, as compared with loss from continuing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of $1,485,911, or $(0.07) per share (basic and diluted), for the year ended December 31, 2019. Our continuing operating income was $1,786,261 for fiscal 2018, or $$(0.09) per share (basic and diluted), for the year ended December 31, 2018.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Income Tax\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For fiscal 2020, we had provision for income tax of $76,343, an increase of $11,728, or 18%, as compared to expense for income tax of $64,615 for fiscal 2019. The increase is primarily due to recording of tax liability of $76,343 and tax liability of $64,615 in relation to uncertain tax positions for the uncertainty surrounding the PRC residency of our non-PRC entities for the years ended December 31, 2020 and 2019.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For fiscal 2019, we had expenses for income tax of $64,615, an increase of $660,036, or 111%, as compared to benefit for income tax of $595,421 for fiscal 2018. The increase is primarily due to recording of tax liability of $64,615 and tax asset of $595,421 in relation to uncertain tax positions for the uncertainty surrounding the PRC residency of our non-PRC entities for the years ended December 31, 2019 and 2018.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gain (loss) from discontinued \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , net of income taxes\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Our gain from discontinued \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was $25,500, or $0.00 per share (basic and diluted), for the year ended December 31, 2020, as compared with a loss from discontinued \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of $76,944, or $(0.00) for the year ended December 31, 2019.Our loss from discontinued \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was $6,626,470, or $(0.31) per share (basic and diluted), for the year ended December 31, 2018.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The summarized operating result of discontinued \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  included our consolidated statements of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is as follows:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                                                         Years Ended December 31,   \par                                                                         2020                                      2019                 2018   \par Revenues                                                                $                          237,431               $   379,630            $   486,244       \par Cost of revenues                                                                                   160,810                   199,888                400,513       \par Gross profit                                                                                       76,621                    179,742                85,732        \par Operating expenses                                                                                 412,686                   196,060                (11,844,769   ) \par Other income (expenses), net                                                                       (45,125    )              (2,240    )            60,499        \par Loss before income tax                                                                             (381,190   )              (18,558   )            (11,698,538   ) \par Income tax expense                                                                                 767                       58,386                 -             \par Loss from discontinued \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                                                                    (322,490   )              (76,944   )            (11,698,538   ) \par Gain from disposal, net of tax                                                                     347,990                   -                      5,072,068     \par Total gain (loss) from discontinued \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , net of income taxes     $                          25,500                $   (76,944   )        $   (6,626,470    ) \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 We realized a gain of $347,990 from the disposal of 100% equity of Anyi Network including its subsidiaries and offset by a loss of $322,490 from discontinued \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the year ended December 31, 2020. As the result, total gain amounted $25,500 from discontinued \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for the year ended December 31, 2020.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 We reclassified Anyi Network and its subsidiaries as discontinued \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and recorded a loss of $76,944 from discontinued \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the year ended December 31, 2019.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 We recognized impairment loss on intangible assets of approximately $2,712,000 when the Company decided to discontinue AGM Belize's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the year ended December 31, 2018.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 We realized a gain of $450,000 from the disposal of 90% equity of AGM Belize with an investment cost basis of $0. The Company also realized a gain of approximately $4,172,000 resulted from 90% of liabilities being assumed by the acquirer pursuant to the equity transfer agreement. Together, the Company recognized a total gain on disposal of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of $5,072,068 for the year ended December 31, 2018.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Net loss\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As a result of the factors described above, our net loss for fiscal 2020 was $1,071,648, compared to net loss of $1,562,855 for fiscal 2019, a decrease in net loss of $491,207, or 31%. Our net loss for fiscal 2018 was $8,412,731, a decrease in net loss of $7,072,596, or 84%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  translation\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The accompanying consolidated financial statements are presented in United States dollar ('$'), which is the reporting \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the Company. The functional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of AGM Holdings, Anyi Technology, Anyi Network, AGM Belize, AGM HK, AGM Software, AGM UK, AGM Australia, AGMClub, and AGM Global are United States dollar. The functional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of AGM Tianjin, its subsidiaries, Jiangsu AnYiWang and its subsidiaries are Renminbi ('RMB'). For the subsidiaries whose functional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are RMB, results of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and cash flows are translated at average exchange rates during the period, assets and liabilities are translated at the exchange rate at the end of the period, and equity is translated at historical exchange rates.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Consolidated Balance Sheets balances, with the exception of equity at December 31, 2020 and 2019, were translated at RMB6.5378 and RMB6.9630 to $1.00, respectively. The equity accounts were stated at their historical rate. The average translation rates applied to the Consolidated Statements of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and Comprehensive Income and the Consolidated Statements of Cash Flows for the years ended December 31, 2020, 2019 and 2018 were RMB6.9003, RMB6.9074 and RMB6.6146 to $1.00, respectively.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Net gains and losses resulting from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  translations are included in the Comprehensive income on the consolidated statements of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . As a result of foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  translations, which are a non-cash adjustment, the Company reported a foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  translation loss of $154,767 for the year ended December 31, 2020. The Company reported a foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  translation gain of $95,060 and $284,923 for the year ended December 31, 2019 and 2018, respectively. This non-cash loss had the effect of increasing our reported comprehensive loss.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 B. Liquidity and Capital Resources.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Liquidity\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For the years ended December 31, 2020 and 2019\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Liquidity is the ability of a company to generate funds to support its current and future \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , satisfy its obligations and otherwise operate on an ongoing basis. As of December 31, 2020 and 2019, we had working capital of $3,663,177 and $4,642,429, including cash and cash equivalents of $664,605 and $1,462,590, respectively. As a result, we believe that our current cash and cash to be generated from our \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\