ed States Code \par              \par 13.2**       Certification of Chief Financial Officer Required by Rule 13a-14(b) and Section 1350 of Chapter 63 of Title 18 of the United States Code \par              \par 101.INS*     XBRL Instance Document. \par              \par 101.SCH*     XBRL Taxonomy Extension Schema Document. \par              \par 101.CAL*     XBRL Taxonomy Extension Calculation Linkbase Document. \par              \par 101.DEF*     XBRL Taxonomy Extension Definition Linkbase Document. \par              \par 101.LAB*     XBRL Taxonomy Extension Labels Linkbase Document. \par              \par 101.PRE*     XBRL Taxonomy Extension Presentation Linkbase Document. \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2      \par *    Filed with this annual report on Form 20-F \par      \par **   Furnished with this annual report on Form 20-F \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SIGNATURES\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The registrant hereby certifies that it meets all of the requirements for filing on Form 20-F and that it has duly caused and authorized the undersigned to sign this annual report on its behalf.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2   AGM GROUP HOLDINGS INC. \par         \par   By:   /s/ Wenjie Tang \par         Name:    Wenjie Tang \par         Title:   Chief Executive Officer(Principal Executive Officer) \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Date: April 22, 2021\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AGM GROUP HOLDINGS INC.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TABLE OF CONTENTS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Consolidated Financial Statements                                                                      \par                                                                                                        \par Reports of Independent Registered Public Accounting Firm                                               F-2 \par                                                                                                        \par Consolidated Balance Sheets as of December 31, 2020 and 2019                                           F-3 \par                                                                                                        \par Consolidated Statements of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and Comprehensive Income for the years ended December 31, 2020, 2019 and 2018    F-4 \par                                                                                                        \par Consolidated Statements of Changes in Equity for the years ended December 31, 2020, 2019 and 2018      F-5 \par                                                                                                        \par Consolidated Statements of Cash Flows for the years ended December 31, 2020, 2019 and 2018             F-6 \par                                                                                                        \par Notes to Consolidated Financial Statements                                                             F-7 \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 F-1\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 REPORT OF INDEPENDENT REGISTERED PUBLIC ACCOUNTING FIRM\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 To:   The Board of Directors and Stockholders of \par       AGM Group Holdings, Inc. \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Opinion on the Financial Statements\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 We have audited the accompanying consolidated balance sheets of AGM Group Holdings, Inc. and subsidiaries (collectively, the 'Company') as of December 31, 2020 and 2019, and the related consolidated statements of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , stockholders' equity, and cash flows for each of the three years ended December 31, 2020, and the related notes (collectively referred to as the financial statements). In our opinion, the financial statements present fairly, in all material respects, the financial position of the Company as of December 31, 2020 and 2019, and the results of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and its cash flows for each of the three years ended December 31, 2020, in conformity with accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Explanatory Paragraph Regarding Going Concern\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The accompanying financial statements have been prepared assuming that the Company will continue as a going concern. As discussed in Note 3 to the financial statements, the Company had incurred substantial losses during the year, which raises substantial doubt about its ability to continue as a going concern. Management's plan in regards to these matters are described in Note 3. These financial statements do not include any adjustments that might result from the outcome of this uncertainty.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Basis for Opinion\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 These financial statements are the responsibility of the Company's management. Our responsibility is to express an opinion on the Company's financial statements based on our audits. We are a public accounting firm registered with the Public Company Accounting Oversight Board (United States) (PCAOB) and are required to be independent with respect to the Company in accordance with the U.S. federal securities laws and the applicable rules and regulations of the Securities and Exchange Commission and the PCAOB.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 We conducted our audits in accordance with the standards of the PCAOB. Those standards require that we plan and perform the audit to obtain reasonable assurance about whether the financial statements are free of material misstatement, whether due to error or fraud. The Company is not required to have, nor were we engaged to perform, an audit of its internal control over financial reporting. As part of our audits, we are required to obtain an understanding of internal control over financial reporting, but not for the purpose of expressing an opinion on the effectiveness of the Company's internal control over financial reporting. Accordingly, we express no such opinion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Our audits included performing procedures to assess the risks of material misstatement of the financial statements, whether due to error or fraud, and performing procedures that respond to those risks. Such procedures included examining, on a test basis, evidence regarding the amounts and disclosures in the financial statements. Our audits also included evaluating the accounting principles used and significant estimates made by management, as well as evaluating the overall presentation of the financial statements. We believe that our audits provide a reasonable basis for our opinion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Critical Audit Matter\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Critical Audit Matter communicated below is a matter arising from the current period audit of the financial statements that was communicated or required to be communicated to the audit committee and that: (1) relates to accounts or disclosures that are material to the financial statements and (2) involved our especially challenging, subjective, or complex judgments. We determined that there are no critical audit matters.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 /s/ JLKZ CPA LLP\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JLKZ CPA LLP\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Flushing, New York\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 April 22, 2021\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 We have served as the Company's auditor since February 2019.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 F-2\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AGM GROUP HOLDINGS, INC.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CONSOLIDATED BALANCE SHEETS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                                                                                        December 31,                    December 31,   \par                                                                                                        2020                            2019           \par                                                                                                                                                       \par ASSETS                                          