\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 5-U.S. stops short of branding Vietnam, Switzerland, Taiwan  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  manipulators\b0\par\par\uc2 984 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 2021\par 13:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds \uc2 Vietnam foreign ministry\uc2  comment)\par \par \uc2 By David Lawder and Andrea Shalal\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON, April 16 (Reuters) - The \uc2 U.S. Treasury Department\uc2  on Friday said Vietnam, Switzerland and Taiwan tripped its thresholds for possible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation under a 2015 U.S. trade law, but refrained from formally branding them as manipulators.\par \par \uc2 In the first semi-annual \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  report issued by Treasury Secretary \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2 , the Treasury said it will commence "enhanced engagement" with Taiwan and continue such talks with Vietnam and Switzerland after the Trump administration labeled the latter two as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulators in December.\par \par \uc2 The Treasury said Taiwan, Vietnam and Switzerland exceeded 2015 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  thresholds during 2020 - a more than $20 billion bilateral trade surplus with the United States, foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  exceeding 2% of gross domestic product and a global current account surplus exceeding 2% of GDP.\par \par \uc2 Despite the finding, it found insufficient evidence under an earlier 1988 law to conclude that Vietnam, Switzerland or Taiwan are manipulating exchange rates to gain a trade advantage or prevent balance of payments adjustments.\par \par \uc2 "For calendar year 2020, we have not made a finding regarding the manipulation designation," a Treasury official told reporters, adding: "We don't view this as a mixed message."\par \par \uc2 The move takes some pressure off Switzerland and Vietnam by lifting the manipulator designation for at least six months.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  (SNB) denied it manipulates the franc and said the report will not alter its monetary policy. "In view of the economic situation and the ongoing high value of the Swiss franc, the SNB remains ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if necessary," it said.\par \par \uc2 An official at \uc2 Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the U.S. decision against applying the manipulator label showed continued good communication between Taipei and Washington on the issue and that U.S. authorities understood Taiwan's "special situation."\par \par \uc2 Taiwan's tech-focused exports to the United States, including laptops and semiconductors, soared in 2020 due to the work-from-home boom sparked by the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 FLEXIBLE POLICY\par \par \uc2 In a statement on Saturday, the \uc2 State Bank of Vietnam\uc2  said it will continue to pursue a flexible exchange rate policy that is managed in a way to contain inflation, ensure macro-economic stability and not to create an unfair trade advantage.\par \par \uc2 Vietnam's foreign ministry said in a later statement it welcomed the Treasury's decision, adding: "Vietnam will maintain dialogues and consultancy with the U.S. over this issue."\par \par \uc2 A Treasury official said it was possible for countries to meet the tests under the "mechanical" 2015 law and not be manipulating their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost exports.\par \par \uc2 He said the report's findings took into account the massive trade and capital flow distortions of the pandemic and the fiscal and monetary policy choices governments took in response.\par \par \uc2 Without the pandemic, the results would have likely been quite a bit different, including for the three economies that hit the engagement triggers, the official added.\par \par \uc2 The Treasury report also said the COVID-19 crisis was likely to continue to affect current account positions over the next year as recoveries accelerated in some economies and lagged in others, adding that these changes were cause for concern.\par \par \uc2 "Treasury is working tirelessly to address efforts by foreign economies to artificially manipulate their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  values that put American workers at an unfair disadvantage," Yellen said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The enhanced engagement includes formal talks to urge Vietnam, Switzerland and Taiwan to develop plans with specific actions to address underlying causes of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  undervaluation and external imbalances, the Treasury said.\par \par \uc2 The talks will also help the Treasury determine the reasons for the three trading partners to make substantial \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 For Taiwan, it said it would initiate enhanced engagement in line with the Trade Facilitation and Trade Enforcement Act of 2015. It expects those talks to help determine if Taiwan manipulated its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  under the 1988 law.\par \par \uc2 MEXICO, IRELAND MONITORED\par \par \uc2 The Treasury said no other major U.S. trading partner met the relevant 1988 or 2015 legislative criteria for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation or enhanced analysis during the review period.\par \par \uc2 It urged \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to improve transparency regarding its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  activities, the policy objectives of its exchange rate management regime, the relationship between the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  activities of the state-owned banks, and its activities in the offshore yuan market.\par \par \uc2 It also said it found 11 economies warrant placement on its "Monitoring List" of major trading partners that merit close attention to their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  practices: China, Japan, South Korea, Germany, Ireland, Italy, India, Malaysia, Singapore, Thailand, and Mexico. All except Ireland and Mexico were included in the December 2020 report to Congress.\par \par \uc2 Reaction in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was muted, with the Swiss franc modestly stronger and the Mexican peso only slightly weaker.\par \par \uc2 Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it did not see an impact on business flows or its ability to implement macroeconomic policies to safeguard domestic stability after remaining on the U.S. monitoring list.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Thailand\uc2  maintains the country has never used the exchange rate as a tool to gain an unfair trade advantage, Assistant Governor \uc2 Chantavarn Sucharitakul\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Thierry Wizman, global interest rates and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Macquarie Group\uc2 , said: "This strikes me as a political decision, not a rules-based decision," adding the Treasury appeared to be trying to determine the intent of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies.\par \par \uc2 "It sounds like the administration is trying not to offend allies here ... those allies that are going to be most important in containing China," Wizman said. (Reporting by David Lawder and Andrea Shalal; Additional reporting by Saqib Ahmed and Kate Duguid in New York, John Revill in Zurich, Ben Blanchard in Taipei and Khanh Vu in Hanoi; Editing by Kim Coghill and David Holmes) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-4-17T12:46:25.000Z 