h, as it was the first to emerge from the pandemic.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it was ready to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par the market to keep the weakening rupiah steady. The\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was down 0.3% on Friday.\par     Yields on Indonesian 10-year bonds rose 3.50\par basis points to 6.641%, while stocks dipped 0.1%.\par Indonesia has some of the highest-yielding debt in emerging\par markets. \par     In the Philippines, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said a spike in\par inflation to its fastest rate in 26 months was temporary,\par suggesting it was not in a rush to reverse its accommodative\par monetary policy stance.\par     Stocks and the peso were flat. \par         \par     HIGHLIGHTS:\par     ** Malaysia's 3-year benchmark yield up 11.4 basis points at\par 2.157%\par     ** Thai oil and gas producer \f28 \uc2 \f2 PTT Pcl\f28 \uc2 \f2  rose 2.5% \par     ** Analysts at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2  say inflation will now start to rank\par higher on the priority list of central banks in emerging markets\par     \par   Asia stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 0344 GMT\par  COUNTRY      \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RIC      \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  YTD  INDEX    STOCKS   STOCKS\par                           DAILY %  %                DAILY %  YTD %\par  Japan                    +0.05    -4.34            -1.97    3.33\par  China                    -0.04    +0.85            -0.36    0.51\par  India                    +0.00    +0.32            0.00     7.86\par  Indonesia                -0.28    -1.82            -0.11    5.09\par  Malaysia                 -0.27    -1.13      