news conference \u8226\'20\'22 09:00 \uc2 Norway \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announces interest rate decision followed by presser \u8226\'20\'22 16:00 \uc2 ECB\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Isabel Schnabel speaks in Frankfurt \u8226\'20\'22 12:00 BOE announces rate decision and publishes minutes of meeting, Bank Rate seen steady at 0.10% Commentary and Analysis USD/JPY heavy, crosses better bid despite risk in neutral \u8226\'20\'22 USD/JPY remained heavy in Asia and in its longer-term downtrend \u8226\'20\'22 Asia 103.56 into Tokyo fix on importer buys before falling back to 103.30 \u8226\'20\'22 103.18/20 double bottom Nov 6/9, 103.00 test may be imminent with USD weak \u8226\'20\'22 Bids from Japanese importers, investors likely to trail down \u8226\'20\'22 Talk of some stops sub-103.15 and 103.00 mixed in however \u8226\'20\'22 JPY crosses steady to bid despite neutral risk mood, Nikkei near par @26,792 \u8226\'20\'22 EUR/JPY 126.07-29 EBS, well within recent higher range \u8226\'20\'22 AUD/JPY also buoyant in recent higher range, Asia 78.24-53 EUR buoyant, EUR/USD to 1.2213, EUR/JPY steady in range \u8226\'20\'22 EUR/USD up marginally from 1.2189 to 1.2213 EBS in Asia, best since Apr '18 \u8226\'20\'22 Broad USD weakness still main factor, better EZ data yesterday helping \u8226\'20\'22 Continues to move up with Ichi tenkan, today 1.2135, underlying support \u8226\'20\'22 EUR/JPY steady after dip to 125.73 EBS yesterday, today 126.08-29 \u8226\'20\'22 Cross likely to remain in recent higher range, capped at 126.73 high 12/10 \u8226\'20\'22 \uc2 ECB\uc2  policy on hold, easy, only recent move on dividends AUD/USD-Jobs beat forecasts, fresh trend high, 0.7638 beckons \u8226\'20\'22 Flat - 0.7567-0.7591 range, moderate volumes - strong jobs had little impact \u8226\'20\'22 Aus jobs beat forecasts, on successful coronavirus control \u8226\'20\'22 Economic uncertainty on COVID-19 has reduced the impact of data on AUD \u8226\'20\'22 Charts; 5, 10 & 21 daily, weekly and monthly moving averages trend north \u8226\'20\'22 Strong and unusual bullish setup targets 0.7638, 38.2% 2011-2020 fall \u8226\'20\'22 Close below 0.7501, 10 DMA a base on this move, would undermine bias \u8226\'20\'22 Upper 21 day Bolli at 0.7610, as overbought signals unwind - trends north GBP/USD-Bid into BoE - expected on hold into Brexit finale \u8226\'20\'22 +0.15% at the top of a 1.3499-1.3530 range, but only light interest \u8226\'20\'22 BoE expected to stay on hold into the Brexit decision \u8226\'20\'22 Crisis at UK ports hits retailers and food manufacturers \u8226\'20\'22 Port disruption could be a taste of things to come in 2021 \u8226\'20\'22 Charts; range holds - daily momentum studies base, 5, 10 & 21 DMAs climb \u8226\'20\'22 1.3525 rising upper 21 day Bollinger band suggests overbought short term \u8226\'20\'22 Positive setup targets 1.3677, 76.4% 2018-2020 fall longer term \u8226\'20\'22 This week's 1.3270 low then 1.3135 low last week initial key supports BOJ policy likely on hold but \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  buys in focus The \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  is likely to keep monetary policy on hold at the end of its board meeting on Friday as fiscal stimulus helps to keep the economy on track, but its surprising decision to buy $6 billion from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely a bigger focus for markets. The MOF is responsible for Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, and technically the BOJ can only buy \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  from MOF. Also, it is the BOJ that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market but at the behest of MOF. With Japan unlikely to dig into its reserves to fill BOJ coffers with dollars, the BOJ (with MOF's blessing) will buy USD from the market without adversely affecting daily flows. To this end, the BOJ said related buys will occur over the course of the fiscal year ending next March. There are some however who believe this might enable the BOJ to purchase USD to stem or slow further falls in USD/JPY in a form of 'stealth' \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Of interest Friday will also be the BOJ's latest economic forecasts, following the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 's slightly improved outlook Wednesday, which may have been behind its decision to leave most policy settings on hold. The BOJ could take a similar tack, especially if the latest outlook is better, though it will no doubt continue to pay lip service to easing more if needed. Additions to US \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  watchlist find comfort in neighbours The \uc2 U.S Treasury\uc2 's long-delayed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  report released Wednesday added Thailand, India and Taiwan to the monitoring list, but has barely elicited a market reaction. Their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are likely to remain stable despite the declining dollar, as they join five other Asian countries that have been on, with no obvious repercussions. \uc2 Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would continue maintaining exchange rate stability. Meanwhile, South Korea and \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , already on the watchlist, have kept up occasional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to subdue recent substantial gains. The Treasury report also named Switzerland and Vietnam as manipulators of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  issued a blunt rebuttal, while \uc2 Vietnam's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  denied trying to create a trade advantage. China was labelled a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator in August 2019, but that was lifted the following January. The \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2 's judgement is likely more bark than bite, for now. It could be used as leverage in future trade talks, but the risk of the Commerce Department imposing countervailing duties based on the report seems slim. The incoming Biden administration probably won't want to inflame global trade wars. Sell the greenback if you will, especially with the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's bleak view on inflation, but don't bet on the new joiners to the watchlist allowing more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation anytime soon. AUD/USD fends off China tensions in sign of strength The Australian dollar's resilience to the deterioration in trade and diplomatic ties with its largest trading partner, China, is a sign of intrinsic strength that should ensure its uptrend continues. As China's insatiable appetite for iron ore, Australia's main export to the country, shows few signs of abating, Aussie bulls have looked past the war of words and widening trade disputes in recent months. China iron ore prices are hovering near a record high, having surged 114% year-to-date on a combination of robust demand and supply concerns. This will create a budget windfall for the Australian government as it earns record amounts from iron ore exports . The trade in iron ore is of vital importance to both nations and hence the chances of it being targeted by either party are negligible, removing a major threat to the Aussie's uptrend. Unprecedented government stimulus programmes and accommodative \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies worldwide should continue to drive the rally in metals and commodities in 2021, with AUD/USD a direct beneficiary. AUD/USD is headed for a test of resistance at 0.7638, the 38.2% of retracement of the 2011-2020 drop. A break opens a rally to 0.7910, the 100-month moving average.\par \par \uc2 To read our latest \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  news and analysis services, click on\par \par \u