\par\par \b \uc2 EM  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Unlikely to Materially Extend Gains -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,407 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2020\par 16:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2020, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 1054 ET - The South African rand and many other emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have strengthened on the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  's monetary policy easing and China's economic recovery, but any further gains are likely to be limited, \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  says. Analysts at the Danish bank say these \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  could appreciate further in the first quarter as economies reopen but considers the "better part of emerging market strength to be behind us." The analysts recommend "utilising these levels to lock in emerging market income, especially in countries where the rate differential has narrowed, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has strengthened since March and where commodities or inflation are a key theme in the economy and \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." They suggest locking in income for 2021 in the rand. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1030 ET - China's EUR4 billion, triple-tranche euro-denominated bond issuance attracted large demand and enabled China to take advantage of the continued low rates environment, says Christophe Cretot, head of debt origination and advisory for Asia-Pacific at Credit Agricole CIB. China sold five-, 10- and 15-year euro-denominated bonds, with the five-year bond priced at a negative yield. "The success of the transaction proves China's credit strength and its enhanced infrastructure connectivity with global financial markets," Cretot says. (emese.bartha@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1027 ET - \uc2 Mohamed El-Erian\uc2  , chief economic advisor at \uc2 Allianz\uc2 , says the global recovery next year will be "uneven, uncertain and unequal." El-Erian , at a \uc2 Moody's\uc2  event, also says companies that survive will grow stronger, gaining pricing power and market share, while weaker firms will get weaker. He also believes the world will move away from globalization and remake supply chains. Global central banks will remain "pedal to the metal" to bolster economies because the risks of not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  exceeds the risks of providing support through monetary policy, El-Erian says. (micah.maidenberg@wsj.com; @MicahMaidenberg)\par \par \uc2 1021 ET - Investors scrambled to snatch up new euro-denominated Chinese government bonds Wednesday but "some signals in the corporate space point to troubles ahead," says Althea Spinozzi, fixed income strategist at \uc2 Saxo Bank\uc2  . "Industrial corporate yields spiked this month signalling more defaults, which might ultimately weigh on the financial system," she says. A spike in government bond yields, due to hefty supply, might further deteriorate corporate spreads, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might not have any other option than to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , she adds. \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  issued for the first time in a year EUR4 billion in euro-denominated debt maturing in five, 10 and 15 years, with the shorted-dated paper pricing at a negative yield after bids for the three-way deal totalled over EUR17 billion.(lorena.ruibal@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1018 ET - The Swiss franc may weaken versus the euro next year but gains will be limited as the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  eases its monetary policy further, \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  says. The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  may be able to "take its foot off the pedal somewhat" in its efforts to curb the franc's appreciation if risk appetite continues to improve on the prospect of coronavirus vaccines, \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  's \uc2 Jane Foley\uc2  says. "The bad news for the \uc2 SNB\uc2  is that in the current environment the number of other G10 central banks fighting disinflation or deflation have increased." The \uc2 ECB\uc2  is expected to increase asset purchases in December, she says. \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  expects EUR/CHF to rise to 1.09 by next summer from 1.0802 currently. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0955 ET - Sterling extends its losses after the EU 's chief Brexit negotiator \uc2 Michel Barnier\uc2  said trade deal talks with the U.K. will be suspended after one of his colleagues tested positive for coronavirus. Barnier said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  that Brexit negotiations will be suspended for a "short period" and the "teams will continue their work in full respect of guidelines." GBP/USD falls 0.5% to a two-day low of 1.3198, according to \uc2 FactSet\uc2 . EUR/GBP rises 0.3% to 0.8956. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0933 ET - The U.K. is likely to need more stimulus to prop up its economy, says \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  . "We expect further fiscal easing to support the recovery, and further public investment," says \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  's \uc2 Jacob Nell\uc2  and Bruna Skarica. After the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  pumped another extra GBP150 billion to its bond-purchasing program in November, they say less action is expected from the monetary policy committee next year. Still, the bank rate is likely to be cut to 0% in February, which opens the door to negative interest rates later in the year, though this isn't the bank's base case. (lorena.ruibal@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0914 ET - S&P Global Ratings has downgraded \uc2 Deutsche Lufthansa AG\uc2  's credit rating further into junk territory as a steep decline of up to 80% in air passenger traffic in 2020 continues to hammer the German airline's finances. The company faces "significant redundancy payments," the rating agency says. This has led S&P to trim \uc2 Lufthansa\uc2  's credit rating to BB- from BB, with a negative outlook. "The negative outlook reflects our view of persisting material uncertainties about the recovery of \uc2 Lufthansa\uc2  's financial metrics and risks of further weakening due to potentially slower-than-expected demand recovery for air passenger travel and insufficient cost-cuttings," it says. S&P had already downgraded \uc2 Lufthansa\uc2  's rating by one notch in July. (lorena.ruibal@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0907 ET - Developed market government bonds offer close to no, and often negative, returns and "clearly offer less defence against future shocks," says \uc2 Andrew Jackson\uc2  , head of fixed income at \uc2 Federated Hermes\uc2 . The value of credit risk premium and illiquidity premiums is meaningful, however, and offers excellent risk adjusted value, Jackson says. He adds that fixed income remains one of the asset classes where it's still possible to deliver significant 'alpha', or the excess return relative to the return of a benchmark index. (emese.bartha@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0844 ET - Sage Group's guidance for revenue and operating-profit margin, as well as its exit-rate annualized recurring revenue, will be in focus when the company reports fiscal 2020 results on Friday, \uc2 UBS\uc2  says. The U.K. accounting-software specialist is expected to report a 7.5% rise in organic recurring revenue and a 2.9% rise in total sales, with operating margin at 21.8%, according to consensus estimates cited by \uc2 UBS\uc2  . For fiscal 2021, guidance for a "low-to-mid single digit" or perhaps 3%-5% recurring revenue growth may be given, but the key question is what margin Sage expects, \uc2 UBS\uc2  says. Consensus forecasts for Sage's fiscal 2021 operating margin currently sit at 22.0%, the bank says. (adria.calatayud@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0842 ET - The South African rand briefly pares losses against the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left its key interest rate unchanged at 3.5%. Two policymakers voted for a rate cut of 25 basis points while three preferred to hold the rate. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor \uc2 Lesetja Kganyago\uc2  said the rate path indicates no further cuts in near term and two increases of 25 basis points in the third and fourth quarters of 2021. Inflation is expected to be "well contained" over the medium term, remaining below but close to the mid point of the target range in 2021 and 2022, he said. USD/ZAR falls to around 15.4748 after the rate decision from 15.5212 beforehand. It last trades up 0.7% on the day at 15.5612. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0801 ET - The \uc2 Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  's decision to raise its key one-week repo rate by 475 basis points to 15% Thursday may not be enough to deliver a sustained lira recovery, \uc2 TD Securities\uc2  says. "As the effective tightening of the weighted average cost of funding is only 20bps today, the [\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] may have to deliver more in the coming months to keep TRY on an appreciation trajectory," TD strategist \uc2 Cristian Maggio\uc2  says. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may need to lift the key rate by another 200-500 basis points to bring inflation under control, he says. However, raising rates to between 17% and 20% would "also be detrimental" for economic activity in the medium-term given the impact of coronavirus, he says. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 19, 2020 10:54 ET (15:54 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020201119egbj002ga\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
