\par\par \b \uc2 Signs of Trouble For Chinese Companies Despite Blockbuster Euro Bond Sale -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,478 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2020\par 16:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2020, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 1021 ET - Investors scrambled to snatch up new euro-denominated Chinese government bonds Wednesday but "some signals in the corporate space point to troubles ahead," says Althea Spinozzi, fixed income strategist at \uc2 Saxo Bank\uc2  . "Industrial corporate yields spiked this month signalling more defaults, which might ultimately weigh on the financial system," she says. A spike in government bond yields, due to hefty supply, might further deteriorate corporate spreads, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might not have any other option than to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , she adds. \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  issued for the first time in a year EUR4 billion in euro-denominated debt maturing in five, 10 and 15 years, with the shorted-dated paper pricing at a negative yield after bids for the three-way deal totalled over EUR17 billion.(lorena.ruibal@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1018 ET - The Swiss franc may weaken versus the euro next year but gains will be limited as the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  eases its monetary policy further, \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  says. The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  may be able to "take its foot off the pedal somewhat" in its efforts to curb the franc's appreciation if risk appetite continues to improve on the prospect of coronavirus vaccines, \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  's \uc2 Jane Foley\uc2  says. "The bad news for the \uc2 SNB\uc2  is that in the current environment the number of other G10 central banks fighting disinflation or deflation have increased." The \uc2 ECB\uc2  is expected to increase asset purchases in December, she says. \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  expects EUR/CHF to rise to 1.09 by next summer from 1.0802 currently. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0955 ET - Sterling extends its losses after the EU 's chief Brexit negotiator \uc2 Michel Barnier\uc2  said trade deal talks with the U.K. will be suspended after one of his colleagues tested positive for coronavirus. Barnier said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  that Brexit negotiations will be suspended for a "short period" and the "teams will continue their work in full respect of guidelines." GBP/USD falls 0.5% to a two-day low of 1.3198, according to \uc2 FactSet\uc2 . EUR/GBP rises 0.3% to 0.8956. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0933 ET - The U.K. is likely to need more stimulus to prop up its economy, says \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  . "We expect further fiscal easing to support the recovery, and further public investment," says \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  's \uc2 Jacob Nell\uc2  and Bruna Skarica. After the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  pumped another extra GBP150 billion to its bond-purchasing program in November, they say less action is expected from the monetary policy committee next year. Still, the bank rate is likely to be cut to 0% in February, which opens the door to negative interest rates later in the year, though this isn't the bank's base case. (lorena.ruibal@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0914 ET - S&P Global Ratings has downgraded \uc2 Deutsche Lufthansa AG\uc2  's credit rating further into junk territory as a steep decline of up to 80% in air passenger traffic in 2020 continues to hammer the German airline's finances. The company faces "significant redundancy payments," the rating agency says. This has led S&P to trim \uc2 Lufthansa\uc2  's credit rating to BB- from BB, with a negative outlook. "The negative outlook reflects our view of persisting material uncertainties about the recovery of \uc2 Lufthansa\uc2  's financial metrics and risks of further weakening due to potentially slower-than-expected demand recovery for air passenger travel and insufficient cost-cuttings," it says. S&P had already downgraded \uc2 Lufthansa\uc2  's rating by one notch in July. (lorena.ruibal@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0907 ET - Developed market government bonds offer close to no, and often negative, returns and "clearly offer less defence against future shocks," says \uc2 Andrew Jackson\uc2  , head of fixed income at \uc2 Federated Hermes\uc2 . The value of credit risk premium and illiquidity premiums is meaningful, however, and offers excellent risk adjusted value, Jackson says. He adds that fixed income remains one of the asset classes where it's still possible to deliver significant 'alpha', or the excess return relative to the return of a benchmark index. (emese.bartha@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0844 ET - Sage Group's guidance for revenue and operating-profit margin, as well as its exit-rate annualized recurring revenue, will be in focus when the company reports fiscal 2020 results on Friday, \uc2 UBS\uc2  says. The U.K. accounting-software specialist is expected to report a 7.5% rise in organic recurring revenue and a 2.9% rise in total sales, with operating margin at 21.8%, according to consensus estimates cited by \uc2 UBS\uc2  . For fiscal 2021, guidance for a "low-to-mid single digit" or perhaps 3%-5% recurring revenue growth may be given, but the key question is what margin Sage expects, \uc2 UBS\uc2  says. Consensus forecasts for Sage's fiscal 2021 operating margin currently sit at 22.0%, the bank says. (adria.calatayud@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0842 ET - The South African rand briefly pares losses against the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left its key interest rate unchanged at 3.5%. Two policymakers voted for a rate cut of 25 basis points while three preferred to hold the rate. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor \uc2 Lesetja Kganyago\uc2  said the rate path indicates no further cuts in near term and two increases of 25 basis points in the third and fourth quarters of 2021. Inflation is expected to be "well contained" over the medium term, remaining below but close to the mid point of the target range in 2021 and 2022, he said. USD/ZAR falls to around 15.4748 after the rate decision from 15.5212 beforehand. It last trades up 0.7% on the day at 15.5612. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0801 ET - The \uc2 Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  's decision to raise its key one-week repo rate by 475 basis points to 15% Thursday may not be enough to deliver a sustained lira recovery, \uc2 TD Securities\uc2  says. "As the effective tightening of the weighted average cost of funding is only 20bps today, the [\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] may have to deliver more in the coming months to keep TRY on an appreciation trajectory," TD strategist \uc2 Cristian Maggio\uc2  says. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may need to lift the key rate by another 200-500 basis points to bring inflation under control, he says. However, raising rates to between 17% and 20% would "also be detrimental" for economic activity in the medium-term given the impact of coronavirus, he says. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0740 ET - The South African rand is likely to be little moved by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy decision later Thursday when it's expected to leave its benchmark interest rate unchanged at 3.5%, \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  says.The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will probably maintain its "wait and see" approach for now due to concerns about the inflationary impact of higher electricity and "other administered prices" as well as a potential depreciation of the rand resulting from increased fiscal risks, Commerzbank \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst Elisabeth Andreae says. "The rand is unlikely to be affected significantly by an unchanged key rate as this seems largely priced in on the market." USD/ZAR rises 0.2% to 15.4871. The rate decision is expected at 1300 GMT.(renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0738 ET - Despite a record decline in gross domestic product, eurozone trade is holding up relatively well, \uc2 UBS\uc2  says. The resilience of net trade has two explanations: exports and imports have suffered almost equal declines and the Covid-19 crisis has mainly hit services, which have a smaller weight in trade than goods, the Swiss bank says. Goods represent 72% of eurozone trade, while services only 28%. \uc2 UBS\uc2  forecasts eurozone GDP will contract by 3% in the fourth quarter, a less severe drop than in spring due partly to the resilience of trade. "Since mobility restrictions are currently less strict outside Europe, and the eurozone industrial sector remains open for business, eurozone export growth should hold up better than during to the spring lockdown," it says. (maria.martinez@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0653 ET - \uc2 Nestle\uc2  's EUR1.5 billion three-part bond deal offers a "core holding" for debt investors given the firm's proven resilience during the pandemic, \uc2 CreditSights\uc2  says. The initial price talk for the new 5-, long 12- and 20-year bonds has been set at mid-swaps +45 bp (implied yield of 0%), +55 bp (implied yield of about 0.4%) and 65 bp (implied yield of about 0.7%), respectively, it says. "We estimate new issue concessions of between 25 bp for the 5-year and up to 40 bp for the new 20-year," the research firm. Concession is the extra yield new bonds usually pay over existing similar debt issued by the company. (lorena.ruibal@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 19, 2020 10:21 ET (15:21 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020201119egbj002gx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
