\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 China conditions the application of the swap\b0\par\par\uc2 1,320 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 By Carlos Burgue\u241\'00\'F1o cburgueno@ambito.com.ar Argentina may use all or part of the u$18.6 billion of the Chinese swap that remain in the reserves, but under conditions that complicate it. As a first definition, and for "contract" reasons, \uc2 Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2  will only be able to count on the tranche of the loan that corresponds to the period of government of \uc2 Cristina Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez de Kirchner\uc2 . Good money anyway, as it reaches about $11 billion, and wouldbe left over to bring peace of mind to argentina's financial market; at least until March when the payment for the 2021 field settlements should reach the public coffers. And in time for the pandemic scouring to begin to loosen to the pace of the long-awaited vaccine. However, another problem in order to execute the loan is another requirement that comes from China.\par \par \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2 , in his September 29 conversation with \uc2 Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2 , was clear and direct and enabled him to use that money to sustain Argentina's economy. However, when the technicians of the two countries began negotiations to see how potential aid would be implemented; problems began. China requires, as an indispensable condition, that the exchange rate be from pesos to yuan, without going through the dollar. Or, eventually euros, but in a minimum amount. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the Republic of China\uc2  made it clear that it wants to take care of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and that it does not want \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  that show a subordination of the Chinese to the American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market demonstrates the true price of the yuan against the dollar, at least for the Western world. For the Chinese government this point is key: its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is more than \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and with clockwork mechanisms so that it is never known seriously and with certainty what the real comparison against the dollar would be. More in times of dialectical and monetary warfare between \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2  and the Donald Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 Argentina would then be obliged not to be able to automatically convert the yuan of the reserves into dollars. You should opt for two paths: triangulation through China's authorized international markets or focus on the trade market with the eastern country. The first case is somewhat risky and financially ruinous, as it would demand high costs and determine million-dollar losses in the level of reserves. The second is more viable, but will depend on the goodwill of private people who trade foreign trade between the country and China. In the case of exporters, the Government would again fall for talking to the sobering and cereal brookers, who have almost a monopoly on the sale of commodities (especially soybeans) from Argentina to China. In the case of importers, we would be talking about billions of dollars in parts, inputs, machinery and final products that the country buys from China. The Government might also think of a third option: to ask for some kind of international dollar credit, based on Argentine foreign trade with China; a possible transaction, common in large international markets, but which will depend on the degree of confidence that the country achieves in the most important banks of the international capital market so that they can take over the transaction. Trade volume with China is high. According to the latest available figures, in the first eight months of the year it was exported to the eastern market for about US$4,016 million and imported for US$5,049 million; Withnegative balance of $1.033 million.\par \par \uc2 It would be the way to take advantage of \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2 's generous offer to \uc2 Alberto Fernandez\uc2 . The President of the People's Republic of China had given him the freeway to use the swap; even releasing its automatic renewal if 12 months after its qualification, Argentina cannot meet its payment.\par \par \uc2 With this novelty transmitted by \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2 , it will be up to the Government whether or not it is enabled; and the amount of such implementation. If the theory of the president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Miguel Pesce, is followed, its use will be given only in the face of extreme need; and with the certainty that the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will understand that it applies to the coming arrival of good news that deserves to make that decision. Otherwise, they understand in the economic cabinet, having all or part of the deposit for about $18.6 billion to control the dollar market, it would exacerbate the crisis, encouraging a "destitting financial blow from the speculative market."\par \par \uc2 Those times of September 2018 are in the memory; when, two years ago, Luis Caputo was finishing his job as president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , having made use of about $2,500 from the "Stand By" signed with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ) to try to contain the dollar. On 24 September Caputo resigned, having spent that money without making significant gains in terms of exchange market control; having also used the "silver bullet" of the possibility of using dollars from the agreement with the Fund to stabilize the exchanger's square. After that situation, for Macri's government everything went downhill until the fateful PASO in August 2019.\par \par \uc2 Sometime in recent weeks, the BCRA and the economic cabinet discussed the possibility of applying some of that Chinese money to increase liquid reserves, close to us$7 billion. The idea was to take that money to a level above $10 billion, and from there start executing restrictive policy for access to the savings dollar. But with a more strong position in front of the market. It was thought that this money, plus the implementation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy from the BCRA and the National Social Security Administration (ANSES) through the placement of dollars from eventual sales of the globals 2035; should guarantee the state a firepower strong enough to discipline any attempt at high speculation. However, the alternative was shelved.\par \par \uc2 A "swap" is a mechanism by which Argentina and \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  undertake to eventually enable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange, without the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of third \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; in this case, the dollar. The capital contribution is made by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of China\uc2 , under the certainty that the original yuan will eventually be used. Meanwhile, until the change is executed, they remain freely available to the depositor. In this case, the BCRA. The first such agreement was signed in 2009 during Mart\u237\'00\'EDn Redrado's presidency at BCRA, to strengthen safeguards in the face of possible international crises and when reserves reached the record of 15% of GDP. In total, that closed agreement was about $10.2 billion to three years, with the option of extending the deadline. Redrado negotiated it with his Chinese peer, \uc2 Zhou Xiaochuan\uc2 , to agree on an exchange of coins that both countries could order from each other and which should then be repaid. The operating permits for the BCRA were extensive. Yuan could be converted into dollars in international markets, or directly used for bilateral exchange. Or, if not, keep them as part of the nominated reserves in the Us \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The second movement with China was activated in the third quarter of2014, during the management of \uc2 Axel Kicillof\uc2  in Econom\u237\'00\'EDa and Juan Carlos F\u225\'00\'E1brega in the BCRA, for about $3.8 billion, transferred in the last quarter of that year. The novelty of this \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  was that it was justified under the beginning of the works for the lifting of the Dam Santacruce\u241\'00\'F1a Cepernic-Kirchner that the Chinese construction company Gezouba had won in tender in partnership with the local Cordoba Electroengineering. The total agreement was about $11 billion, in successive settlements dependent on the progress of the works. This would be the money that, in the event of force majeure, could be used by \uc2 Alberto Fernandez\uc2 's government to have more weapons in its war against \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.\par \par \uc2 Filed.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020201028egas003rg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
