\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2 's Message: Freeway to Use Swap\b0\par\par\uc2 784 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 By Carlos Burgue\u241\'00\'F1o cburgueno@ambito.com.ar \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2  was clear and direct with \uc2 Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2 , at the time of giving him a concrete signal yesterday about Argentina's macroeconomic situation. The president of the People's Republic of China, in telephone conversation with the local head of state, although without going into detail, gave him a free way to use the "swap" agreed between the central banks of both countries. It even released its automatic renewal if 12 months after its qualification, Argentina cannot meet its payment. In addition, as long as the loan is used, there will be no need to tie it to foreign trade between the two states or to the payment to Chinese suppliers in local public works; the source of the accounting credit between the eastern country and Argentina.\par \par \uc2 With this novelty transmitted by \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2 , it will be up to the Government whether or not it is enabled; and the amount of such execution. If the theory of the president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Miguel Pesce, is followed, its use will be given only in the face of extreme need; and with the certainty that the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will understand that it applies to the coming arrival of good news that deserves to make that decision. Otherwise, they understand in the economic cabinet, having all or part of the deposit for about $18.6 billion to control the dollar market, it would exacerbate the crisis, encouraging a "destitting financial blow from the speculative market."\par \par \uc2 Those times of September 2018 are in the memory; when, two years ago, Luis Caputo was finishing his job as president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , having made use of about $2,500 from the "Stand By" signed with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ) to try to contain the dollar. On 24 September Caputo resigned, having spent that money without making significant gains in terms of exchange market control; having also used the "silver bullet" of the possibility of using dollars from the agreement with the Fund to stabilize the exchanger's square. After that situation, for Macri's government, everything went downhill until the fateful PASO in August 2019.\par \par \uc2 Sometime in recent weeks, the BCRA and the economic cabinet discussed the possibility of applying some of that Chinese money to increase liquid reserves, close to us$7 billion. The idea was to take that money to a level above $10 billion, and from there start executing restrictive policy for access to the savings dollar. But with a more strong position in front of the market. It was thought that this money, plus the implementation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy from the BCRA and the National Social Security Administration (ANSES) through the placement of dollars from eventual sales of the globals 2035; should guarantee the state a firepower strong enough to discipline any attempt at high speculation. However, the alternative was shelved.\par \par \uc2 A "swap" is a mechanism by which Argentina and \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  undertake to eventually enable \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , without the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of third \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; in this case, the dollar. The capital contribution is made by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of China\uc2 , under the certainty that the original yuan will eventually be used. Meanwhile, until the change is executed, they remain freely available to the depositor. In this case, the BCRA. The first such agreement was signed in 2009 during Mart\u237\'00\'EDn Redrado's presidency at BCRA, to strengthen safeguards in the face of possible international crises and when reserves reached the record of 15% of GDP. In totalthat closed agreement was for about $10.2 billion to three years, with the option of extending the deadline. Redrado negotiated it with his Chinese peer, \uc2 Zhou Xiaochuan\uc2 , to agree on an exchange of coins that both countries could order from each other and which should then be repaid. The operating permits for the BCRA were extensive. Yuan could be converted into dollars in international markets, or directly used for bilateral exchange. Or, if not, keep them as part of the nominated reserves in the Us \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The second movement with China was activated in the third quarter of 2014, during the management of \uc2 Axel Kicillof\uc2  in Econom\u237\'00\'EDa and Juan Carlos F\u225\'00\'E1brega in the BCRA, for about US$3.8 billion, transferred in the last quarter of that year. The novelty of this \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  was that it was justified under the beginning of the works for the lifting of the Dam Santacruce\u241\'00\'F1a Cepernic-Kirchner that the Chinese construction company Gezouba had won in tender in partnership with the local Cordoba Electroengineering. The total agreement was about $11 billion, in successive settlements dependent on the progress of the works.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020200930eg9u0018c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
