ed. Implied volatility, which is a key in pricing options and a bellwether of future actual volatility, has seen its benchmark one-month expiry contract drop back to 6.75 from a 7.15 peak Wednesday. However, one-week expiry options remain elevated in the mid 8s for now - recognising short-term volatility risk from the impending \uc2 European Union\uc2  summit, but not so much Thursday's \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . One-month expiry risk reversals show the implied volatility premium for EUR calls over puts (topside vs downside strikes) has also eased to 0.25 from 0.35. As well as EUR/USD consolidation, big topside barriers options are maintaining an element of supply in the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  options market. EUR/USD implied volatility: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/2C6zDFT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://tmsnrt.rs/2C6zDFT}}}\uc2  1-3-12-month EUR/USD risk reversals: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3fKM5ta"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://tmsnrt.rs/3fKM5ta}}}\uc2  China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  looks like a prudent investment China's yuan is carefully managed, which means it is not prone to unexpected or large movement, and that reduces \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk significantly. For a relatively high-yield \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a zero-rate world, that should encourage traders to buy. Fundamentals also offer reason to buy the yuan. China's economy has quickly shaken off the impact of the coronavirus, in contrast to what's happening elsewhere, especially in the United States. Given the current disparity in economic performance, China looks set to close the gap with the United States The yuan seems cheap -- it's recovered little of the losses incurred since March's turmoil. Unlike the yuan, major commodities and China's stocks have soared, boosting the probability of a CNH rise. And the yuan's safe. China tightly controls movement, but CNH is liquid and free to trade. The 200-day moving average has capped CNH for seven days. Respect a break. Trade weighted CNH: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/2Ovg50g"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://tmsnrt.rs/2Ovg50g}}}\uc2  To read our latest \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  news and analysis services, click on\par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-7-19T11:23:38.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200716eg7g01w7l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
