\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Anti-dumping administrative investigation procedure on imports of textured textile filament polyester originating in China and India is declared to start\b0\par\par\uc2 26,359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 DOF: 31/03/2020\par \par \uc2 RESOLUTION accepting the request for an interested party and declaring the initiation of the anti-dumping administrative investigation procedure on imports of textured textile filament polyester originating in the People's Republic of China and the Republic of India, regardless of the country of origin.\par \par \uc2 Download PDF\par \par \par \par \uc2 On the sidelines a stamp with the National Shield, which says: United Mexican States.- Secretariat of Economy.RESOLUTION BY WHICH THE REQUEST OF INTERESTED PARTY IS ACCEPTED AND THE START OF THE ADMINISTRATIVE PROCEDURE OF ANTIDUMPING RESEARCH ON THE IMPORTATIONS OF FILAMENTO TEXTIL TEXTURIZED INDEPENDENTLY OF THE COUNTRY OF PROCEDENCEVisto to resolve at the start stage the administrative file 22/19 based in the International Trade Practices Unit (UPCI) of the Secretariat of the Economy (the "Secretariat"), this Resolution is issued in accordance with the followingRESULTANDOSA. Application1. \u160\'00\'A0On 31 October 2019, Akra Polyester, S.A. de C.V. (Akra or the "Applicant") requested the initiation of the administrative investigation procedure for unfair international trade practices, in its form of price discrimination, on imports of textured textile filament polyester (PFTT) originating in the People's Republic of China ("China") and the Republic of India ("India"), irrespective of country of origin. 2.\u160\'00\'A0Akra argued that over the past three years, in particular in the period July 2018-June 2019, imports into Mexico of PFTT originating in China and India increased significantly in price discrimination, and their increase in absolute terms and in relation to Apparent Domestic Consumption caused material injury to the domestic industry. This damage was reflected in negative effects on the main indicators, particularly in a significant reduction in domestic merchandise prices, resulting in not only loss of market share but also in sales, generating lower-than-expected revenue, thus affecting desirable outcomes, jeopsing the viability of the national PFTT-producing industry. It proposed as a period of investigation from 1 July 2018 to 30 June 2019 and as a period of injury analysis from 1 July 2016 to 30 June 2019. It presented the arguments and evidence in order to support its request, which are contained in the reference file, which were considered for the issuance of this Resolution. 3.\u160\'00\'A0On 9 January 2020, the Applicant responded to the Prevention made to it by the Secretariat on 26 November 2019 in order to clarify, correct or supplement various aspects of its application. B. Applicant4. \u160\'00\'A0Akra is a company incorporated under Mexican law. Its main activity is the manufacture of all kinds of synthetic, artificial, cellular or any other type of fibers, including any kind of finishing, processing and textured, that can be made to such fibers. He pointed out as an address to receive notifications the one located in Paseo de la Reforma No. 222, Torre 1, Piso 17, Col. Ju\u225\'00\'E1rez, C.P. 06600, Mexico City. C. Product under investigation1.\u160\'00\'A0Overview5. \u160\'00\'A0Akra noted that the subject merchandise is knownalso such as continuous yarn of textured textile filament or textured polyester yarn (PTY, it is a synthetic continuous multifilament yarn made from polyglatthalate (PET) polyester, whether virgin or recycled, which is manufactured through a textured process that imparts special properties to yarn filaments, including elasticity, thickness, strength, moisture absorption, insulation, as well as the appearance of a natural fiber. He added that the coverage of the investigated product includes all forms of PFTT, regardless of surface texture or appearance, density and thickness of yarn (measured in denier or decitex), number of filaments, number of layers, finish (lustre or gloss), cross section, color, dyeing method, texturing method, or packaging method (such as spindles, tubes or rollers); because while PFTT may vary in terms of denier, luster and color, they do not change its essential characteristics. 2. Features 6. \u160\'00\'A0Akra noted that all PFTT shares the same physical and chemical characteristics, because it is a commodity, which is manufactured from polyester (obtained from virgin or recycled PET), is composed of continuous filaments and has a textured surface that imparts specific properties, including elasticity, thickness, strength, moisture absorption, and insulation; in addition to a cotton-like softness that is demanded in many end uses, including the manufacture of fibers that come into contact with people such as clothing, home textiles and tapestries, bedding and automotive seats;\u160\'00\'A0in addition to that it is also used in industrial applications such as medical materials and devices, industrial materials, and general automotive applications. 7.\u160\'00\'A0Akra indicated that the main physical and chemical properties, as well as generally accepted technical specifications identifying PFTT yarns are decitex or denier, the number of filaments, brightness or luster and the level of braiding (intermingle), which are distinguished from yarns made from other raw materials with different physical characteristics. 8.\u160\'00\'A0To support its arguments, Akra submitted screenshots of Internet pages of various PFTT producers with information from PFTT manufactured in China and India, as well as a copy of the \uc2 United States International Trade Commission\uc2 (USITC) resolution on the preliminary stage of the anti-dumping investigation by PFTT originating in China and India, published in December 2018 ("2018 USITC Resolution"), which states that the PFTT is characterized by its denier, yarns, brightness, and other variants associated with the texturing process and that the Applicant's customers generally acquire it with denier between 20 and 400, although such merchandise may be manufactured in denier outside this range according to the specifications requested by each customer. 3. Tariff treatment9. \u160\'00\'A0Akra indicated that the product under investigation enters the domestic market through tariff fraction 5402.33.01 of the General Import and Export Tax Act (TIGIE) Tariff, the description of which is as follows:Tariff codingDescriptionChapter 54 Synthetic or artificial componentsPartive 5402Sying of synthetic filaments (except sewing thread) without conditioning for retail sale, including synthetic monofilaments of a degree less than 67 decitex \u8211\'20\'13Textured yarn:Subheading 5402.33\u8211\'20\'13PolyestersPromrynry duty 5402.33.01Of polyestersSource: Tariff Information System Via the Internet (SIAVI).10.\u160\'00\'A0According to SIAVI information, the Secretariat noted that imports of PFTT entering by TIGIE's 5402.33.01 fraction are subject to a general ad valorem tariff of 5%, with the exception of imports originating in countries with which Mexico has concluded free trade agreements, which are duty-free, and imports originating in Japan and Vietnam, which have a tariff of 2% and 3%, respectively. 11.\u160\'00\'A0The unit of measurement used in TIGIE and commercial \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the kilogram. 4. Production process12. \u160\'00\'A0Akra indicated that PFTT is produced from polyester, which is manufactured in a polymerization reactor, whose raw materials of origin are purified terephthalic acid (PTA) and monoethylene glycol (MEG) or recovered material (recovered or recycled PET chips or granules). Once produced, the liquid polyester can be spinning directly (direct spinning) or passed into solid state (cooling and cutting into small granules) to be then spun into extruders by pressure and temperature.\u160\'00\'A0The yarn produces partially oriented yarn (POY), which can have different characteristics such as thickness and filaments depending on the grips used. Finally, the POY moves to texturing machines, which give the final finish by stretching, temperature and textured. PFTT production process diagram\par \par \uc2 13.\u160\'00\'A0The Applicant also noted that the inputs used in the production of PFTT are the PTA and MEG, whether you have a polymerization reactor, or granulated polyester, if it was generated directly from the chemical reaction of the raw materials or if it comes from a process with recycled or recovered PET material. 14.\u160\'00\'A0To support it, Akra submitted a copy of the 2018 USITC Resolution, as well as information obtained from Internet pages of PFTT producers, both from China and India, concerning their production processes (including their diagrams); In addition, a specialized opinion in the textile field, which includes both the description and diagrams confirming the production process of the PFTT. 5. Standards 15. \u160\'00\'A0Akra indicated that by virtue of the huge variety of final characteristics of the fabrics, such as the construction, composition, density, weight, touch, appearance, comfort, durability, abrasion resistance, breakage, heat treatment, exposure to light, among others, and the wide range of variants in dyeing and textile finishing processes, the establishment of standard values for THE PFTT specifications is not due to generally accepted local or international standards, so even though the research PFTT produced by different producers may have variations in their specifications, such differences do not prevent them from being commercially substitutable, because the equipment for their manufacture, raw materials and production processes are directed to the same end-use. 6. Uses and functions16. \u160\'00\'A0Akra noted that PFTT is mainly used in the textile industry to manufacture various fabrics, ribbons, ropes, embroidery, sewing yarn that are incorporated into various types of fabrics, which are intended to make garments (pants, sportswear, socks, etc.), from the home (mattress, upholstery, ornamentals), of the industry(indoor coatings) and for other diverse uses. To support the above, it submitted a copy of the 2018 USITC Resolution, as well as information obtained from Internet pages of PFTT producers from both China and India, concerning the uses of PFTT producers. D. Interested Parties17. \u160\'00\'A0The possible parties available to the Secretariat that might have an interest in appearing in this investigation are:1. ImportadoresAdient M\u233\'00\'E9xico Automotriz, S. de R.L. de C.V.Blvd. \uc2 Johnson Controls\uc2  No. 1993Pase Santa Mar\u237\'00\'EDaC.P. 67190, Monterrey, Nuevo Le\u243\'00\'F3nAlitex, S.A. de C.V.Circuit de la Industria No. 109Ler industrial park LermaC.P. 52000, Lerma de Villada, State of MexicoAnsertex, S.A. de C.V.Av. Federal M\u233\'00\'E9xico-Puebla Km. 21.7Col. La PazC.P. 56400, Los Reyes Acaquilpan, State of MexicoApolo Textil, S.A. de C.V. Calle 8 Pte. No. 701Col. LibertadC.P. 72000, Puebla, PueblaArturo Calder\u243\'00\'F3n OrnelasHortensia No. 55Col. Lomas de San MiguelC.P. 52928, Atizap\u225\'00\'E1n de Zaragoza, State of MexicoAunde M\u233\'00\'E9xico, S.A. de C.V.Calle C, Mn C, Lt. 1Santa Ana XalmimilulcoC.P. 74169, Huejotzingo, PueblaAvances Modernos, S.A. de C.V.Bosques de Ciruelos No. 160, floor 3, Of. 301-bCol. Forest of the LomasC.P. 11700, Mexico CityA&Z Global, S.A. de C.V.Morelos s/nCol. Tlanalapa CentroC.P. 43930, Tlanalapa, HidalgoAztextil, S.A. de C.V.Calle De Los Granjenos No. 7Col. YuririaC.P. 38940, Yuriria, GuanajuatoBarcel\u243\'00\'F3 Calcetines, S.A. de C.V.Carretera La Gachupina Km. 1Col. CentroC.P. 38400, Valle Santiago, GuanajuatoBeg