\par\par \b \uc2 PRECIOUS-Gold eases from near 2-week high on \uc2 China  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  stimulus\b0\par\par\uc2 505 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2020\par 14:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices)\par \par \uc2 * Further rallies in gold will need fresh impetus-analyst\par \par \uc2 * Gold in euros hit record peak of 1,463.98 euros/oz\par \par \uc2 * Trading subdued due to the U.S. holiday\par \par \uc2 * Dollar hovers close to a four-month peak\par \par \uc2 By Sumita Layek\par \par \uc2 Feb 17 (Reuters) - Gold prices on Monday eased from a near two-week high, as a monetary policy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to limit the economic impact from the coronavirus outbreak reassured investors and boosted demand for higher-risk assets.\par \par \uc2 Spot gold was down 0.2% to $1,581.33 per ounce at 1255 GMT. U.S. gold futures shed 0.1% at $1,584.40.\par \par \uc2 "While the optimism in stock markets is rather evident that this outbreak may be transitory and that a pivot point is near, however the gold investors are yet not willing to join whole heartedly in the equities game," said FXTM market analyst \uc2 Han Tan\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Gold earlier in the session was hovering near Friday's near two-week high of $1,584.65, but pared gains as global shares rose after China cut the interest rate on its medium term loans in an attempt to counteract the economic hit from the epidemic.\par \par \uc2 This comes after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early February announced an injection of 1.2 trillion yuan ($174 billion) worth of liquidity into the markets.\par \par \uc2 The dollar hovered close to a four-month peak scaled in the previous session, making gold relatively expensive for holders of other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Given that gold prices remain elevated above $1,550's and that Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  remain weaker to the U.S. dollar ... it shows that there is still a fair amount of concern among investors about the potential fallout for the global economy from this outbreak," Tan said.\par \par \uc2 Gold in euros hit a record peak of 1,463.98 euros per ounce earlier in the session.\par \par \uc2 The virus outbreak has claimed 1,770 lives so far and has threatened economic growth in the world's second largest economy.\par \par \uc2 Major Asian financial hubs too are grappling with the impact from the virus as the public health crisis pushed Singapore to downgrade its 2020 economic growth forecast and has heightened the risk of recession in Japan.\par \par \uc2 "The main trend remains positive but for further rallies we would need some fresh impetus, as stock markets are still in a risk on scenario," ActivTrades chief analyst Carlo Alberto De Casa said in a note.\par \par \uc2 "The first resistance is now placed at $1,585, followed by $1,592 and by the psychological threshold of $1,600."\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, palladium rose 1.8% to $2,475.64 an ounce, silver was up 0.4% at $17.79, while platinum gained 0.5 to $967.83.\par \par \uc2 Trading is expected to be subdued as financial markets in the United States will be shut for a public holiday. (Reporting by Sumita Layek in Bengaluru. Editing by Jane Merriman) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-2-17T14:05:47.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200217eg2h01of1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
