\par\par \b \uc2 PRECIOUS-Gold falls 1% as China works to stem economic impact of virus\b0\par\par\uc2 524 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 2020\par 20:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices)\par \par \uc2 * Gold to stay in $1,550-$1,600/oz range for now - analyst\par \par \uc2 * Palladium jumps more than 4%\par \par \uc2 * U.S. factory orders rise above expectations\par \par \uc2 By Diptendu Lahiri\par \par \uc2 Feb 4 (Reuters) - Gold slid more than 1% on Tuesday as China's steps to mitigate the economic impact of the coronavirus epidemic drove some investors away from safe havens and back into riskier assets.\par \par \uc2 Spot gold fell 1.61 % to $1,550.69 per ounce by 1:40 p.m. EST (1840 GMT), after hitting its lowest since Jan. 21 at $1,548.70. U.S. gold futures settled down 1.7% at $1,555.50.\par \par \uc2 "The dramatic move in global equity markets, especially in the U.S. markets, clearly indicates there is lesser concern about coronavirus denting GDP and we have a lesser need for safe havens," said David Meger, director of metals trading at High Ridge Futures.\par \par \uc2 Wall Street built on a recovery in world stocks as fresh \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  calmed investor nerves.\par \par \uc2 Beijing's efforts included signing off on more government spending, tax relief and subsidies for virus-hit sectors, policy sources said.\par \par \uc2 The outbreak has undermined the country's economic activity as cities are locked down, with travel restrictions and businesses closed.\par \par \uc2 Further, the dollar strengthened, making gold more expensive for buyers holding other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, some uncertainty remained about the extent of the impact on the Chinese and global economies.\par \par \uc2 "In case the impact of the virus is less than the market has priced in, it could lead to a correction in gold prices, but as long as we don't see economic growth accelerate, gold prices will remain supported," said Quantitative Commodity Research analyst Peter Fertig.\par \par \uc2 Some traders have also started to price in a cut to U.S. interest rates by June.\par \par \uc2 Lower interest rates reduce the opportunity cost of holding the non-yielding bullion.\par \par \uc2 Gold should stay within a range of $1,550 to $1,600 an ounce ahead of more political and economic headlines, \uc2 George Gero\uc2 , managing director at RBC Wealth Management, said in a note.\par \par \uc2 On the economic front, new orders for U.S.-made goods rose 1.8%\u8203\'20\'0B\u8203\'20\'0B in December, beating analysts' consensus forecast of a 1.2% gain.\par \par \uc2 India's gold imports in January plunged 48% from a year earlier as a rally in local prices near record highs prompted buyers to curtail purchases, a government source said.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, palladium gained 4.5% to $2,423.76, after touching its highest since Jan. 24 at $2,435.\par \par \uc2 "Now that optimism has returned to financial markets, it seems that market participants have forgotten their fears of how the spread of the coronavirus might affect demand," \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  analysts said in a note.\par \par \uc2 "Nonetheless, the consequences for China, the main consumer of palladium, are likely to be very serious."\par \par \uc2 Silver fell 0.5% to $17.57, while platinum dipped 0.4%, to $962.83. (Reporting by Diptendu Lahiri and Sumita Layek in Bengaluru; Editing by Richard Chang and Tom Brown) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-2-4T20:00:20.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200204eg2402ybu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
