\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Gold falls 1% after China's efforts to curb coronavirus's economic impact\b0\par\par\uc2 285 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 By Diptendu Lahiri\par \par \uc2 Feb 4 (Reuters) - Gold fell by more than 1% on Tuesday, as China's measures to mitigate the economic impact of the coronavirus epidemic took some investors away from safe assets.\par \par \uc2 * Spot gold lost 1.61% to $1,550.69 per ounce at 1840 GMT, after reaching its lowest level from January 21 to $1,548.70. U.S. gold futures, meanwhile, fell 1.7 percent to $1,555.50.\par \par \uc2 * "The big movement in global stock markets, especially in the U.S. market, clearly indicates that there is less concern about the coronavirus's decline in GDP and that we need less need to seek refuge," he said David Meger, director of metals trading at High Ridge Futures.\par \par \uc2 * Major Wall Street indices were up Tuesday for the second day in a row, as a new \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seemed to calm investor satters.\par \par \uc2 * The coronavirus outbreak has undermined China's economic activity because several cities are quarantined, amid travel restrictions and business closures.\par \par \uc2 * In addition, the dollar strengthened in the session and made gold more expensive for buyers with other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * In macroeconomic matters, new orders for goods manufactured in the United States in December had their biggest rise in nearly a year and a half thanks to strong demand for defense aircraft, but weak business spending on equipment points to a margin limited uptick in manufacturing.\par \par \uc2 * In other precious metals, palladium gained 4.5% at $2,423.76 per ounce, silver fell 0.5% to $17.57 and platinum fell 0.4% to $962.83.\par \par \uc2 (Edited in Spanish by Rofdrigo Charme)\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020200204eg24005mw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
