\par\par \b \uc2 CANADA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  DEBT-Canadian dollar steadies near 2-month low as China adds liquidity\b0\par\par\uc2 361 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 2020\par 15:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Canadian dollar rises 0.1% against the greenback\par     * Loonie trades in a range of 1.3268 to 1.3301 \par     * Price of U.S. oil increases 2.6%\par     * Canadian bond yields rise across a steeper yield curve\par \par     TORONTO, Feb 4 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar edged higher\par against the greenback on Tuesday as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tempered concern about the economic impact of the\par coronavirus outbreak, with the loonie steadying after it hit a\par two-month low the day before.\par     Stocks          rallied globally after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of\par China\f28 \uc2 \f2  injected liquidity into money markets, while the price of\par oil, one of Canada's major exports, rallied on hopes for new\par output curbs from \f28 \uc2 \f2 OPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  and its allies to offset any potential\par drop in demand triggered by the virus. U.S. crude oil futures\par        were up 2.6% at $51.41 a barrel.                         \par     At 8:52 a.m. (1352 GMT), the Canadian dollar          was\par trading 0.1% higher at 1.3279 to the greenback, or 75.31 U.S.\par cents. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which hit a two-month low on Monday at\par 1.3302, traded in a range of 1.3268 to 1.3301.    \par     Trade confidence among Canadian exporters fell to its lowest\par level in nearly a decade, Canada's export credit agency said, as\par businesses wrestle with protectionist policies and fret about\par the global economy.             \par     Canadian trade data for December is due on Wednesday and the\par January jobs report is awaited on Friday, both of which could\par guide expectations for the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Canada\f28 \uc2 \f2  interest rate outlook.\par     Last month, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  left the door open to\par an interest rate cut should a recent slowdown in domestic growth\par persist. Money markets see about a 60% chance that it will ease\par by April.                \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Canadian government\f28 \uc2 \f2  bond yields rose across a steeper yield\par curve, with the 10-year yield             rising 5.2 basis\par points to 1.310%. On Monday, it hit its lowest intraday level in\par nearly four months at 1.252%.      \par \par  (Reporting by Fergal Smith; Editing by Steve Orlofsky)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-2-4T15:11:17.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200204eg2402hcp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
