\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Coronavirus carries the dollar close to $800 and opens debate about reviving  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 754 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 With the signing of the U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade agreement, uncertainty in global markets had become significantly widened. However, the sudden appearance of the coronavirus and the consequences it has brought with it, caused this trend towards the normalization of expectations to be rapidly reversed.\par \par \uc2 This chest of the way in the external plane also had implications for the domestic side. The main effect was seen in the volatile exchange rate hike. This, because yesterday, after exceeding $800 at half a session, the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  finally closed at $796.38, which in turn represented a slight increase of 0.56% from the close of last day when it scored $791.92.\par \par \uc2 It is also the highest level of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since last December 3, when it reached $803.3. Since the beginning of the year, the dollar has risen $40 and the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the most depreciated in the world after the Jamaican dollar.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, copper, impacted precisely by market fear salutation about the greater fragility of China's economy because of the coronavirus, caused it to collapse to its lowest level since 4 October last year. With this, the spot value of the red metal fell 1.35% to US$2.54 at the end of the day and completed 10 consecutive sessions of descents, in which it accumulated a 10.8% retracement.\par \par \uc2 This also represents its biggest negative streak since November 5, 2015 and November 19, 2015 when it dropped for 11 straight sessions.\par \par \uc2 Faced with this scenario, and concerned about the deterioration of domestic economic conditions and the direct impact at the local level, the Minister of Finance, \uc2 Ignacio Briones\uc2 , entered the subject fully to express his concern. "We know that the price of copper is very exposed to the swings of the world economy (...) we had good news on this matter just nine days ago, copper had had a major hike after the Chinese-US signs of agreement, and then, on the issue of the virus affecting that country, there are signs of concern. That impacts the markets, if this could decrease Chinese activity and that's what we're seeing today, illustrating the volatileness of the issue," he explained.\par \par \uc2 Experts debateIn the midst of the bullish escalation of the exchange rate, experts disagree on the forward-looking behavior of the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and also discuss the next steps the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should take in the face of eventual trend maintenance Bullish. This, after the issuing institute halted the sale of dollars in early January.\par \par \uc2 Against this backdrop, Banchile economist Agust\u237\'00\'EDn Garc\u237\'00\'EDa sees that "the dollar can continue to climb, to the extent that events that generate uncertainty are not controlled." He believes that "globally, if fears of the coronavirus are not allayed, the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will remain a haven for market players." A similar view is that Banco Santander economist Sindy Olea says that "emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are likely to continue depreciating and, consequently, the exchange rate may continue to scale and return to $800."\par \par \uc2 On what the next steps should be of the Central, the chief economist of Bci Studies, Sergio Lehmann, argued that "on the basis that the issuing body has used as the main argument to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  the exchange rate volatility and not the level, for now there is no good foundation for resuming the sale of dollars in the spot market. In the same vein, Olea remained who, in addition to discarding, for now, the option of an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said that "unlike November, the factors that explain much of the depreciation are related to developmentsexternal external slabs."In contrast, Garc\u237\'00\'EDa de BanChile believes that "it is possible that the Central could resume the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would change if the dollar persistently exceeds the $800 barrier, because the real exchange rate would reach the levels that motivated the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcement November"\par \par \uc2 IPSA posts new dropThe IPSA, meanwhile, fell 0.5% in yesterday's day. Among the biggest declines are Sonda, with 2.4%; Bank of Chile, with 2.38% and Concha Toro, with 2.10%. This behavior was also shown in line with major global exchanges, which were declining as the day progressed.\par \par \uc2 In the month, the Santiago Stock Exchange is the fourth most falling dollar measure in the world.\par \par \uc2 The Coronavirus entry carries the dollar close to $800 and opens debate about reviving \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was first published in The Third.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020200131eg1v001ur\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
