\par\par \b \uc2 Nordic Morning Briefing: Calmer Day Ahead With Earnings and German Data Due\b0\par\par\uc2 1,305 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 2019\par 06:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2019, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR - All times GMT \par  \par Nordic Macro \par 0730 Sweden September Household \par      Lending \par 0730 Sweden September PPI \par 0730 Sweden September Retail Sales \par  \par Other Macro \par 0600 Germany November Gfk Consumer \par      Confidence \par 0800 Germany October Ifo \par 1400 U.S. October \f28 \uc2 \f2 University of \par      Michigan\f28 \uc2 \f2  Confidence \par 1430 \f28 \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  's Villeroy Speaks \par  \par Nordic Equities \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Autoliv Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . 3Q \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Electrolux AB\f28 \uc2 \f2  3Q \par  \par Other Equities \par Anheuser Busch  Inbev NV 3Q \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Aon PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2   3Q \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Verizon Communications Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2  . 3Q \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 VF Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2  . 2Q \par  \par GLOBAL NEWS: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boris Johnson\f28 \uc2 \f2  Calls for Election on Dec. 12:\f28 \par \par \uc2 British Prime Minister \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  called for a snap general election on Dec. 12 in an effort to pressure his political opponents to back his Brexit deal and face him at the ballot box, but opposition lawmakers suggested they wouldn't rise to the bait.\par \par \uc2 The election call was the latest political gamble for a prime minister who after just three months in office unexpectedly secured an agreement with the \uc2 European Union\uc2  last week for a Brexit deal.\par \par \uc2 A motion calling for the election is to be put to the House of Commons on Monday, the government said. To pass, it would need a two-thirds majority and thus require support from the main opposition Labour Party.\par \par \uc2 Labour leader \uc2 Jeremy Corbyn\uc2  said the party would decide how to respond to Mr. Johnson's election pitch once it was clear that the \uc2 European Union\uc2  would extend the Brexit deadline past Oct. 31.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, the party's interim advice to lawmakers was that they would probably recommend abstaining, making the motion all but impossible to pass.\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 Pence Condemns Beijing over Hong Kong But Sounds Optimistic on a China Trade Pact:\par \par \uc2 U.S. Vice President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  on Thursday expressed hope for a near-term trade deal with \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but blasted Beijing for its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Hong Kong and its treatment of Muslim-minority groups.\par \par \uc2 Delivering a speech in Washington, Mr. Pence said President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  believes China wants to make a trade deal soon and that the U.S. is seeking open markets and fair trade.\par \par \uc2 But the vice president's talk took a more critical stance as he offered a rebuke of the world's second-largest economy for what he characterized as actions that "curtail the rights and liberties that Hong Kong's people were guaranteed," and called out abuse of Uighurs and other Muslim-minority groups in the Xinjiang region. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GLOBAL MARKETS: \par  \par EuroSTOXX50 3616.72  -4.00 -0.11% \par DAX 30     12849.20 -26.80 -0.21% \par FTSE 100    7327.70   1.50  0.02% \par Dow        26809.50   4.00  0.01% \par S&P 500     3004.92  -4.50 -0.15% \par Nasdaq 100  7925.60 -38.60 -0.48% \par Futures at 0317 GMT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European stock futures pointed to a mixed start to trading on Friday as investors were likely to seek direction amid a rare quiet news day on the geopolitical front.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In Asia, stocks were similarly subdued as the end of the week approached with the Nikkei and Shanghai Composite flat.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stocks in the U.S. Thursday generally inched higher though the Dow Jones Industrial Average continued to underperform broader benchmarks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A mixed bag of U.S. corporate profit reports offered a murky outlook on the state of the U.S. economy. Traders have braced for weaker results this earnings season amid concerns about the costly trade war between the U.S. and China, and increased signs of slowing economic growth worldwide. Earnings reports in the last couple of weeks have mostly exceeded Wall Street analysts' modest expectations. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IN FOCUS: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It's a calmer day Friday with much thinner earnings and economic calendars.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After a slight overall uptick in September, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nordea\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects the Ifo business climate indicator to fall back again, given that both new orders and business expectations were at their weakest levels since the financial crisis last month.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New orders, especially from abroad, have fallen off a cliff this year, reflecting a lack of demand in the German industry, it added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The ZEW index from October is offering some hope of staying above August levels as it fell less than expected, but sentiment around the current situation remains subdued despite relief from the recent settlement in the trade dispute between the U.S. and China, as Brexit uncertainty is still a drag." \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \par  \par EUR/NOK \par 0350 GMT 10.1521-71 \par Previous 10.1439-89 \par %Chg 0.08 \par  \par EUR/SEK \par 0350 GMT 10.7242-342 \par Previous 10.7187-287 \par %Chg 0.05 \par  \par USD/NOK \par 0350 GMT 9.1438-98 \par Previous 9.1342-402 \par %Chg 0.11 \par  \par USD/SEK \par 0350 GMT 9.6600-90 \par Previous 9.6530-620 \par %Chg 0.07 \par  \par STOCK INDEXES: \par  \par OMXN40  1609.81   -3.29 -0.20% \par OMXS30  1736.98  +11.11 +0.64% \par OBX      835.70  +13.20 +1.60% \par OMXC20  1046.02   +5.43 +0.52% \par OMXH25  4103.07  -32.44 -0.78% \par  \par Brent crude: $61.33 \par  \par  \par NORDIC MARKETS: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nordic stock markets were mixed Thursday after the latest earnings releases produced some huge swings in regional share prices.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nokia\f28 \uc2 \f2  shares traded over 20% lower after slashing guidance. The world's second-biggest telecom-equipment maker was the worst performer in Europe as the growing costs of rolling out gear for 5G mobile networks also forced it to halt its dividend. On the flip side, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Norwegian Air Shuttle\f28 \uc2 \f2  shares flew over 20% higher after signing an aircraft financing deal and beating earnings expectations.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A slew of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central-bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  decisions also provided mixed clues on the state of the global economy. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  left interest rates unchanged and stuck with a plan to start buying bonds next month. The Norwegian and Swedish central banks held their benchmark rates unchanged while \f28 \uc2 \f2 Turkey's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  surprised markets with a bigger-than-expected cut to its key repo rate. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ENERGY: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil prices were lower in Asia, with AxiTrader saying that while oil demand concerns still weigh on the market, sentiment is likely to improve as the U.S. and China continue to make progress in trade negotiations.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, a lift in U.S. business activity may support prices, with U.S. flash manufacturing \f28 \uc2 \f2 PMI\f28 \uc2 \f2  for October beating expectations. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Other Top Stories: \par ================= \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. Weighs Leaving More Troops, Sending Battle Tanks to Syria\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The White House is considering options for leaving about 500 U.S. troops in northeast Syria and for sending dozens of battle tanks and other equipment to protect them, officials said Thursday, the latest in an array of scenarios following President Trump's decision this month to remove all troops there.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ---\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Pence Slams \f28 \uc2 \f2 NBA\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nike\f28 \uc2 \f2  Over China Stance\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vice President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mike Pence\f28 \uc2 \f2  took on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nike\f28 \uc2 \f2  and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Basketball Association\f28 \uc2 \f2  , accusing them of being complicit in China's efforts to curtail democracy in Hong Kong.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ---\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Amazon\f28 \uc2 \f2  's Third-Quarter Profit Slides 26%\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Amazon\f28 \uc2 \f2  's profit machine sputtered again after more than two years of surging growth, weighed down by the tech giant's heavy investment into reducing shipping times for retail customers.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ---\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Saudi-Backed Yemeni Government, Separatists Sign Power-Sharing Deal\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Saudi-backed Yemeni government has signed a power-sharing deal with a local group seeking a separate state in the south, an agreement designed to keep the country from fracturing and pave the way for broader talks to end its five-year-old war.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ---\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Lawmakers Push to Pass Revised Trade Deal as Year's End Approaches\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Lawmakers worry that the window to pass the Trump administration's renegotiated trade deal with Mexico and Canada is closing, and if negotiations don't conclude soon, the pact's prospects could fade against political priorities in the coming election year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Dominic Chopping at dominic.chopping@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones News